+## Thor 蜂窝启动资源
+
+PongPower 在 AP 发布 SMP2P 428 后分别读取 AP 的 STOP 和基带的 READY。NativeUfs 完成 PAS4 元数据回读后可调用 `pong_thor_mss_after_metadata` 再次取样。日志内的负状态保留所缺的分区、共享项或命名端点。
+
+Thor 的 `rproc_ddr` 路径由 HLOS 的 ACV 和 MC0 提供，`crypto_ddr` 还经过 CE0、SN3、SN0 与 SH0。驱动从运行时 CMD DB 解析每项的地址、unit、width 和 VCD。此阶段只读取资源描述，实际带宽请求及其聚合、释放仍待接入。板级路径参照 [MiCode waipio.c](https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/mayfly-s-oss/drivers/interconnect/qcom/waipio.c)。
+
+## Thor v188 candidate PAS4 wait bound
+
+`ThorPas4Kernel.inc` uses one absolute two-second deadline while waiting for a matching secure-firmware wake queue. If that deadline expires, it marks the queue failed and returns transaction error `-2004`. It does not issue RESUME, ACK, a fresh PAS_INIT_IMAGE, or AUTH_AND_RESET after this failure. Metadata, carveout ownership, and any later wake token remain retained for this boot. This prevents an unbounded second `THREAD_UNINT` sleep; it does not establish modem READY or prove the observed desktop freeze is fixed. Host tests and ARM64 compilation are recorded separately from device validation in the candidate release receipt.
+
+## Thor v189 staged ICC admission diagnostics
+
+`ThorModemIccAdmission.h` keeps a fixed-size, read-only inventory of the CMD DB resource descriptions, validated modem demand plans and DDR statistics. `PongPlatformResources.cpp` protects the inventory with `powerLock`, copies one snapshot before logging, and records `result=SKIP` through the existing `PongProbeRecord` API. The current board's `PongProbeRecord` shim is a no-op, so the structured console records and retained diagnostic state do not establish durable panic capture.
+
+The inventory explicitly reports the six required BCMs, active/wake/sleep requirements, inherited baseline coverage, owner coverage, inherited voter and snapshot epoch. CMD DB describes addresses, unit, width and VCD. DDR DRV statistics and reusable TCS command slots do not provide a per-BCM, per-APSS-voter baseline or owner handoff. No new TCS/MMIO read is added. Baseline coverage, owner coverage and epoch remain zero; the inherited voter remains unverified. `authAllowed` is always false, and the PAS gate requires it as well as the existing hold flag. No operation in this diagnostic layer enables ICC admission, writes RPMh or issues AUTH_AND_RESET.
+
+A real admission implementation still needs a documented baseline readback or explicit owner-handoff protocol covering all required resources and active/wake/sleep sets, with a consistent epoch and an inherited APSS voter identity. It must preserve every other owner's contribution and retain ownership through ambiguous completion. VCD batch/commit, acknowledgement and release lifetimes remain future work. A successful resource plan or stable diagnostic sample cannot substitute for that evidence. This source is staged separately from the immutable v188 image and release receipt; no device result is claimed.
+
+## Thor PAS4 SMP2P
+
+At the ICC admission gate, PongPower samples the stock MSS inbound item 435 and outbound APSS STOP item 428 through a read-only mapping. Its console record distinguishes missing entries from clear bits and reports FATAL, READY, HANDOVER, STOP_ACK and SHUTDOWN_ACK from the same inbound word. After an accepted signed PAS4 reset, the READY wait retains one mapping for up to five seconds, logs state changes, and treats a sampled FATAL as a failed boot even if READY is also set. These samples observe levels. The direct watchdog IRQ remains a separate signal.
+
+Immediately before signed PAS4 authentication, the driver checks the current AP STOP and remote item again. It proceeds only when AP STOP is readable and clear and the inbound MSS item is still absent. A peer which becomes visible while segments are loaded retains its ownership.
+
+### Thor v206 staged BCM sampling
+
+At the PAS auth gate the shared power driver samples enabled sleep and wake commands from APSS DRV2 TCS3–6. It validates the observed v2.7 geometry and the six CMD DB addresses, reads commands twice under the AP power lock, and reports unstable, unsupported and duplicate entries. An unobserved resource has unknown state. This samples queued messages only. The active vote and owner admission continue to use their own inputs.
diff --git a/ThorActiveTcs.h b/ThorActiveTcs.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..aa95a9dcad4a995f5fae31f0199bcfda1c58175a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorActiveTcs.h
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+// Thor APSS DRV2. The vendor FDT allocates 3 ACTIVE, 2 SLEEP, 2 WAKE,
+// and 1 FAST_PATH in this order. powerLock serializes every Thor AP sender.
+struct ThorActiveTcs {
+    static constexpr unsigned irqEnable = 0xd00, irqStatus = 0xd04, irqClear = 0xd08;
+    static constexpr unsigned mode = 1u << 16, trigger = 1u << 24;
+    static constexpr unsigned completed = (1u << 16) | (1u << 8);
+    static constexpr unsigned base(unsigned id) { return 0xd00 + id * 0x2a0; }
+    uint32_t version = 0, caps = 0, irqMask = 0, pending = 0;
+    unsigned idleMask = 0, enabledMask = 0, armedMask = 0;
+    bool retained = false;
+    // An ADSP command can leave an entry here. Do not reuse its slot or
+    // resource after an ambiguous result. GPU/board votes retain ACTIVE0.
+    uint32_t pendingArc[3]{};
+    int selected = -1;
+
+    template<class Io>
+    const char *vote(Io &io, uint32_t address, uint32_t value)
+    {
+        return transfer(io,address,value,nullptr);
+    }
+
+    template<class Io>
+    const char *transfer(Io &io, uint32_t address, uint32_t value, uint32_t *response, bool adspWrite = false)
+    {
+        const bool scoped = response || adspWrite;
+        selected = -1;
+        if (retained) return "prior-transaction-retained";
+        caps = io.read(0xc);
+        const unsigned commands = (caps >> 27) & 31;
+        version = io.read(0);
+        const unsigned major = (version >> 16) & 255;
+        if (major == 0 || major >= 3 || ((caps >> 12) & 63) < 8 || !commands || commands > 16)
+            return "layout-unverified";
+
+        if (address && (pendingArc[1] == address || pendingArc[2] == address))
+            return "prior-arc-address-quarantined";
+        pending = io.read(irqStatus);
+        irqMask = io.read(irqEnable);
+        idleMask = enabledMask = armedMask = 0;
+        for (unsigned id = 0; id < 3; ++id) {
+            const unsigned b = base(id);
+            const unsigned enabled = io.read(b + 0x1c);
+            const unsigned ctl = io.read(b + 0x14);
+            const bool idle = io.read(b + 0x18) != 0;
+            if (idle) idleMask |= 1u << id;
+            if (enabled) enabledMask |= 1u << id;
+            if (ctl & ~mode) armedMask |= 1u << id;
+            if (enabled >> commands || (!idle && !enabled && !pendingArc[id])) return "active-state-unverified";
+            for (unsigned i = 0; i < commands; ++i) {
+                if ((enabled & (1u << i)) && io.read(b + 0x34 + 20 * i) == address)
+                    return "active-address-in-use";
+            }
+            if (selected < 0 && !pendingArc[id] && (!scoped || id != 0) && idle && !enabled && !(pending & (1u << id)) && !(ctl & ~mode))
+                selected = int(id);
+        }
+        if (selected < 0) return "no-empty-active-slot";
+        const unsigned b = base(unsigned(selected)), bit = 1u << selected;
+        const unsigned ctl = io.read(b + 0x14);
+        if ((ctl & ~mode) || !io.read(b + 0x18) || io.read(b + 0x1c) || (io.read(irqStatus) & bit))
+            return "active-slot-changed";
+        const unsigned oldWait = io.read(b + 0x10);
+        const bool irqWasEnabled = (io.read(irqEnable) & bit) != 0;
+        // ADSP uses distinct cmd-db resources. A scoped failure retains its
+        // slot and target, including any unconfirmed change to that rail.
+        // Legacy writes keep their original sender-wide uncertain state.
+        if (scoped) pendingArc[selected] = address;
+        else retained = true;
+        unsigned arcDelays = 0;
+        auto pause = [&]() {
+            if (scoped && arcDelays++ >= 200) return false;
+            io.delay();
+            return true;
+        };
+        auto sync = [&](unsigned reg, unsigned data) {
+            io.write(reg, data);
+            for (unsigned n = 0; n < 1000; ++n) {
+                if (io.read(reg) == data) return true;
+                if (!pause()) break;
+            }
+            return false;
+        };
+        if (irqWasEnabled) {
+            io.write(irqEnable, io.read(irqEnable) & ~bit);
+            if (io.read(irqEnable) & bit) return "irq-mask-unconfirmed";
+        }
+        if (!sync(b + 0x14, ctl & ~trigger) || !sync(b + 0x14, 0))
+            return "disarm-unconfirmed";
+        io.write(b + 0x30, response ? 0x108 : 0x10108); // length 8, response requested; only writes set bit 16
+        io.write(b + 0x34, address);
+        if (!response) io.write(b + 0x38, value);
+        io.write(b + 0x10, 1);
+        if (!sync(b + 0x1c, 1) || !sync(b + 0x14, mode)) return "arm-unconfirmed";
+        io.write(b + 0x14, mode | trigger);
+
+        bool progressed = false;
+        for (unsigned n = 0; n < 10000; ++n) {
+            const unsigned status = io.read(b + 0x3c);
+            const bool idle = io.read(b + 0x18) != 0;
+            if (!idle || (status & completed) != completed) progressed = true;
+            else if ((!scoped && progressed) || (io.read(irqStatus) & bit)) {
+                // An ARC baseline must come from this read's IRQ and completed
+                // command. Capture slot zero before retiring it, and publish
+                // nothing to the caller until retirement also succeeds.
+                const uint32_t word = response ? io.read(b + 0x40) : 0;
+                if (!sync(b + 0x14, mode) || !sync(b + 0x14, 0) || !sync(b + 0x1c, 0))
+                    return "retirement-unconfirmed";
+                io.write(irqClear, bit);
+                if ((io.read(irqStatus) & bit) || !sync(b + 0x10, oldWait) || !sync(b + 0x14, ctl))
+                    return "retirement-unconfirmed";
+                if (irqWasEnabled) {
+                    io.write(irqEnable, io.read(irqEnable) | bit);
+                    if (!(io.read(irqEnable) & bit)) return "irq-restore-unconfirmed";
+                }
+                if (scoped) pendingArc[selected] = 0;
+                else retained = false;
+                if (response) *response = word;
+                return nullptr;
+            }
+            if (!pause()) break;
+        }
+        return "response-timeout-retained";
+    }
+};
diff --git a/ThorAdspArcRead.h b/ThorAdspArcRead.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e9d56cf88ec32a99fa41b88d59d10ed5dd20795a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorAdspArcRead.h
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+#include "ThorActiveTcs.h"
+
+// Called under the same powerLock, using the same sender as APSS writes.
+// An ARC resource returns this DRV's own active corner in the response word.
+template<class Io>
+const char *thorAdspArcRead(ThorActiveTcs &sender, Io &io, uint32_t address, uint32_t &corner)
+{
+    if (!address || (address & 3)) return "invalid-arc-address";
+    uint32_t value = 0;
+    const char *error = sender.transfer(io,address,0,&value);
+    if (error) return error;
+    if (value > 15) return "invalid-arc-response";
+    corner = value;
+    return nullptr;
+}
+
+// Caller has identified the board's dedicated lcx.lvl or lmx.lvl resource
+// under powerLock. Its unconfirmed write must never stall unrelated votes.
+template<class Io>
+const char *thorAdspArcWrite(ThorActiveTcs &sender, Io &io, uint32_t address, uint32_t corner)
+{
+    if (!address || (address & 3)) return "invalid-arc-address";
+    if (corner > 15) return "invalid-arc-corner";
+    return sender.transfer(io,address,corner,nullptr,true);
+}
diff --git a/ThorAdspCold.inc b/ThorAdspCold.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..af09c53f5318047fbf6d2779475ce68dadaa6c77
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorAdspCold.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+// Called with Thor TCSR SMEM lock 3 held on cold preparation. A single
+// free-mark store publishes missing AP items. An inherited AP item is reused
+// only if uncached and byte-for-byte cold. Peer-owned items are never adopted.
+static int adsp_partition(const QcomSmem *s, QcomSmemPartition *p)
+{
+    int rc = qcom_smem_partition(s,0,2,p);
+    if (rc) return rc;
+    const uint32_t toc = s->size-0x1000, count = rd(s,toc+8);
+    if (count>(0x1000-TOC_HEADER)/TOC_ENTRY) return QcomSmemNoTable;
+    unsigned matches = 0;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<count;++i) {
+        uint32_t row=toc+TOC_HEADER+i*TOC_ENTRY;
+        uint32_t at=rd(s,row), size=rd(s,row+4), pair=rd(s,row+12);
+        if (!at || !size) continue;
+        if (pair==2 || pair==(2u<<16)) {
+            if (at!=p->offset || size!=p->size) return QcomSmemBadPartition;
+            ++matches;
+        } else if (at<(uint64_t)p->offset+p->size && p->offset<(uint64_t)at+size)
+            return QcomSmemBadPartition;
+    }
+    return matches==1 ? 0 : QcomSmemBadPartition;
+}
+
+static const uint16_t adsp_ids[3]={429,478,479};
+static const uint32_t adsp_sizes[3]={QCOM_SMP2P_ITEM_BYTES,32,0x4000};
+
+/* A valid AP hand-off has exactly the same contents as a fresh publication.
+ * No inherited byte is cleared or rewritten. In particular, refuse every
+ * FIFO cursor, pending payload, restart flag, nonzero STOP or unused entry. */
+static int adsp_idle_ap_item(const QcomSmem *s, unsigned slot, uint32_t at)
+{
+    uint32_t start=0;
+    if (slot==0) {
+        if (rd(s,at)!=QCOM_SMP2P_MAGIC || rd(s,at+4)!=QCOM_SMP2P_VERSION ||
+            rd(s,at+8)!=(2u<<16) || rd(s,at+12)!=(1u<<16|QCOM_SMP2P_MAX_ENTRIES) ||
+            rd(s,at+16) || !mss_signal_name(s,at+20,"master-kernel") ||
+            rd(s,at+32)!=(uint32_t)'l') return 0;
+        start=36;
+    }
+    for (uint32_t off=start;off<adsp_sizes[slot];off+=4)
+        if (rd(s,at+off)) return 0;
+    return 1;
+}
+
+int qcom_smem_adsp_prepare_cold(const QcomSmem *s,QcomAdspColdOwner *owner)
+{
+    if (!owner || owner->part) return QcomSmemInvalidSignal;
+    QcomSmemPartition p;
+    int rc=adsp_partition(s,&p);
+    if (rc) return rc;
+    const uint16_t ids[]={429,478,479,443,480};
+    uint32_t free=rd(s,p.offset+12), cached=rd(s,p.offset+16), needed=0;
+    uint32_t offsets[5]={0};
+    owner->present=owner->blocker=0;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<5;++i) {
+        uint32_t length=0;
+        rc=qcom_smem_find_stable(s,&p,ids[i],&offsets[i],&length);
+        if (rc!=0 && rc!=QcomSmemMissing) return rc;
+        owner->sizes[i]=length;
+        if (rc==0) owner->present|=1u<<i;
+    }
+    for (unsigned i=3;i<5;++i) {
+        if (owner->present & (1u<<i)) { owner->blocker=ids[i]; return QcomSmemExists; }
+    }
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<3;++i) {
+        if (!(owner->present & (1u<<i))) {
+            needed+=ENTRY+align_up(adsp_sizes[i],8);
+            continue;
+        }
+        uint32_t at=0,length=0;
+        if (owner->sizes[i]!=adsp_sizes[i] ||
+            find_mss_uncached(s,&p,free,ids[i],&at,&length) ||
+            at!=offsets[i] || length!=adsp_sizes[i] || !adsp_idle_ap_item(s,i,at)) {
+            owner->blocker=ids[i]; return QcomSmemExists;
+        }
+    }
+    if ((free&7) || free<PART_HEADER || free>cached || cached>p.size)
+        return QcomSmemCorrupt;
+    if (needed>cached-free) return QcomSmemNoSpace;
+    QcomAdspColdOwner fresh=*owner;
+    fresh.part=p.offset;
+    uint32_t next=free;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<3;++i) {
+        if (fresh.present & (1u<<i)) { fresh.items[i]=offsets[i]; continue; }
+        const uint32_t padded=align_up(adsp_sizes[i],8), entry=p.offset+next, data=entry+ENTRY;
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,entry,CANARY|(uint32_t)adsp_ids[i]<<16);
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,entry+4,padded);
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,entry+8,padded-adsp_sizes[i]);
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,entry+12,0);
+        for (unsigned off=0;off<padded;off+=4) qcom_smem_write32(s,data+off,0);
+        fresh.items[i]=data;
+        next+=ENTRY+padded;
+    }
+    if (!(fresh.present & 1)) {
+        const uint32_t out=fresh.items[0];
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,out,QCOM_SMP2P_MAGIC);
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,out+8,2u<<16);
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,out+12,1u<<16|QCOM_SMP2P_MAX_ENTRIES);
+        const char name[16]="master-kernel";
+        for (unsigned i=0;i<16;i+=4) {
+            uint32_t word=0;
+            for (unsigned j=0;j<4;++j) word|=(uint32_t)(uint8_t)name[i+j]<<(8*j);
+            qcom_smem_write32(s,out+20+i,word);
+        }
+        qcom_smem_write32(s,out+4,QCOM_SMP2P_VERSION);
+    }
+    if (next!=free) qcom_smem_write32(s,p.offset+12,next);
+    *owner=fresh;
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int adsp_live_snapshot(const QcomSmem *s,const QcomAdspColdOwner *owner,uint32_t *signals)
+{
+    if (signals) *signals=0;
+    if (!owner || !owner->part) return QcomSmemInvalidSignal;
+    QcomSmemPartition p;
+    int rc=adsp_partition(s,&p);
+    if (rc) return rc;
+    if (p.offset!=owner->part) return 2;
+    uint32_t at=0,length=0;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<3;++i) {
+        rc=qcom_smem_find_stable(s,&p,adsp_ids[i],&at,&length);
+        if (rc) return rc==QcomSmemMissing ? 2 : rc;
+        if (at!=owner->items[i] || length!=adsp_sizes[i]) return 2;
+    }
+    const uint32_t out=owner->items[0];
+    if (rd(s,out)!=QCOM_SMP2P_MAGIC || rd(s,out+4)!=QCOM_SMP2P_VERSION ||
+        rd(s,out+8)!=(2u<<16) || rd(s,out+12)!=(1u<<16|QCOM_SMP2P_MAX_ENTRIES) ||
+        !mss_signal_name(s,out+20,"master-kernel") || (rd(s,out+36)&1)) return 2;
+
+    rc=qcom_smem_find_stable(s,&p,443,&at,&length);
+    if (rc==QcomSmemMissing) {
+        rc=qcom_smem_find_stable(s,&p,480,&at,&length);
+        if (rc!=QcomSmemMissing) return rc ? rc : QcomSmemUnpublished;
+        for (unsigned i=0;i<4;++i) if (rd(s,owner->items[1]+4*i)) return 2;
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (rc) return rc;
+    if (length<20) return QcomSmemInvalidSignal;
+    const uint32_t version=rd(s,at+4),counts=rd(s,at+12);
+    if (!version) return QcomSmemUnpublished;
+    if (rd(s,at)!=QCOM_SMP2P_MAGIC || (version&255)!=1 || rd(s,at+8)!=2 ||
+        (counts&65535)>QCOM_SMP2P_MAX_ENTRIES || (counts>>16)>(counts&65535) ||
+        !fits(20,(counts>>16)*20,length)) return 2;
+    uint32_t bits=0,matches=0;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<(counts>>16);++i) {
+        const uint32_t name=at+20+i*20;
+        if (mss_signal_name(s,name,"slave-kernel")) { bits=rd(s,name+16); ++matches; }
+    }
+    smem_snapshot_barrier();
+    if (rd(s,at+4)!=version || rd(s,at+12)!=counts) return QcomSmemUnstable;
+    if (!matches) return QcomSmemUnpublished;
+    if (matches!=1 || (bits & ((1u<<0)|(1u<<3)|(1u<<7)))) return 2;
+    if (signals) *signals=bits;
+    return bits & (1u<<1) ? 1 : QcomSmemUnpublished;
+}
+
+int qcom_smem_adsp_edge_state(const QcomSmem *s,const QcomAdspColdOwner *owner)
+{
+    return adsp_live_snapshot(s,owner,0);
+}
+
+int qcom_smem_adsp_handover(const QcomSmem *s,const QcomAdspColdOwner *owner)
+{
+    uint32_t signals=0;
+    adsp_live_snapshot(s,owner,&signals);
+    return !!(signals & (1u<<2));
+}
diff --git a/ThorAdspProxy.h b/ThorAdspProxy.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..494b4fe5ef93881525acf970e881e5160dba0136
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorAdspProxy.h
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+#include <stdint.h>
+// All accesses under the DRV2 power lock. A new AP request replaces the
+// captured HLOS baseline only after its own, appropriately clamped write ACK.
+struct ThorAdspProxy {
+    struct Rail {uint32_t addr{},minimum{},limit{},other{},effective{};bool held{};};
+    Rail rail[2]{};
+    bool raised() const {
+        for (const auto &r:rail) if (r.held && r.effective!=r.other) return true;
+        return false;
+    }
+    template<class Read,class Write> bool acquire(Read read,Write write) {
+        for (auto &r:rail)
+            if (r.held || !r.addr || !r.minimum || r.minimum>r.limit || r.limit>15 ||
+                !read(r.addr,r.other) || r.other>r.limit) return false;
+        for (auto &r:rail) {
+            r.effective=r.other<r.minimum?r.minimum:r.other;
+            r.held=true; // A failed acknowledgement may still have reached the remote.
+            if (r.effective!=r.other && !write(r.addr,r.effective)) return false;
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
+    template<class Send> bool client(uint32_t addr,uint32_t value,Send send) {
+        for (auto &r:rail) {
+            if (!r.held || r.addr!=addr) continue;
+            if (value>r.limit) return false;
+            const uint32_t level=value<r.minimum?r.minimum:value;
+            if (!send(level)) return false;
+            r.other=value;r.effective=level;return true;
+        }
+        return send(value);
+    }
+    template<class Read,class Write> bool release(Read read,Write write) {
+        bool ok=true;
+        for (unsigned i=2;i;--i) {
+            auto &r=rail[i-1];
+            if (!r.held) continue;
+            uint32_t live=0;
+            if (!read(r.addr,live) ||
+                (live!=r.other && (live!=r.effective || !write(r.addr,r.other))) ||
+                !read(r.addr,live) || live!=r.other) {ok=false;continue;}
+            r.held=false;
+        }
+        return ok;
+    }
+};
diff --git a/ThorBatteryReading.h b/ThorBatteryReading.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..18c2c44ae6ad60efe21c1d7bbdd4ad3a552603c7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorBatteryReading.h
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include "ShengBattmgr.h"
+
+namespace ThorGauge {
+enum Field : unsigned { Present, Capacity, Status, UsbOnline, FieldCount };
+struct Property { uint32_t opcode, id; };
+constexpr Property fields[FieldCount] = {
+    {SHENG_BATTMGR_OP_BATTERY_GET, 2}, {SHENG_BATTMGR_OP_BATTERY_GET, 4},
+    {SHENG_BATTMGR_OP_BATTERY_GET, 0}, {SHENG_BATTMGR_OP_USB_GET, 0},
+};
+inline uint32_t read32(const uint8_t *p)
+{
+    return uint32_t(p[0]) | (uint32_t(p[1]) << 8) | (uint32_t(p[2]) << 16) | (uint32_t(p[3]) << 24);
+}
+struct Cycle {
+    unsigned cursor = 0;
+    bool sent = false;
+    uint32_t valid = 0, values[FieldCount] = {};
+    void request(uint32_t (&p)[6]) const {
+        p[0] = SHENG_BATTMGR_OWNER;
+        p[1] = SHENG_BATTMGR_TYPE_REQUEST;
+        p[2] = fields[cursor].opcode;
+        p[3] = 0; // battery 0
+        p[4] = fields[cursor].id;
+        p[5] = 0;
+    }
+    bool answer(const uint8_t *p, unsigned n) {
+        if (!sent || cursor >= FieldCount || n != 24 || read32(p) != SHENG_BATTMGR_OWNER ||
+            read32(p+4) != SHENG_BATTMGR_TYPE_REQUEST || read32(p+8) != fields[cursor].opcode ||
+            read32(p+12) != fields[cursor].id) return false;
+        const uint32_t value = read32(p+16);
+        const uint32_t limit[FieldCount] = {1, 10000, 4, 1};
+        if (!read32(p+20) && value <= limit[cursor]) {
+            values[cursor] = value;
+            valid |= 1u << cursor;
+        }
+        ++cursor;
+        sent = false;
+        return true;
+    }
+    bool retireOptional(unsigned &disabled) {
+        if (cursor < Status || cursor >= FieldCount) return false;
+        disabled |= 1u << cursor;
+        ++cursor;
+        sent = false;
+        return true;
+    }
+    void skipDisabled(unsigned disabled) {
+        while (cursor < FieldCount && (disabled & (1u << cursor))) ++cursor;
+    }
+    bool has(Field f) const { return (valid & (1u << f)) != 0; }
+    bool measured() const { return has(Present) && values[Present] == 1 && has(Capacity); }
+    unsigned percent() const { return (values[Capacity] + 50) / 100; }
+};
+// Require a new peer VERSION at the start of an otherwise unowned AP transport.
+// Resuming firmware-owned AP FIFO indices would steal another client's channel.
+inline bool initialVersion(const uint32_t (&d)[4], uint32_t txBytes, uint32_t rxBytes, uint32_t header) {
+    return txBytes == 0x4000 && rxBytes == 0x4000 && !d[0] && !d[1] && !d[2] &&
+        d[3] >= 8 && d[3] < rxBytes && !(d[3] & 7) && header == (1u << 16);
+}
+}
diff --git a/ThorBatterySource.cpp b/ThorBatterySource.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..29fb155878a11fd16c7a71377151195dd6e78b1f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorBatterySource.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,367 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+// Thor's APSS/ADSP private SMEM edge, as described by cape-adsp-pas in the shipping DT.
+// A bounded, nonblocking boot probe never loads firmware or resets an existing AP edge.
+#include <IOKit/IOLib.h>
+#include <IOKit/IODeviceMemory.h>
+#include <IOKit/IOPlatformExpert.h>
+#include <IOKit/pwr_mgt/IOPMPowerSource.h>
+#include <libkern/c++/OSDictionary.h>
+#include <kern/clock.h>
+#include <kern/thread.h>
+#include <libkern/OSKextLib.h>
+#include <mach/kmod.h>
+#include <pexpert/pexpert.h>
+#include "PongPlatformResources.h"
+#include "QcomGlink.h"
+#include "QcomScm.h"
+#include "QcomSmem.h"
+#include "QcomSmp2p.h"
+#include "ThorBatteryReading.h"
+
+extern kmod_info_t g_kernel_kmod_info;
+extern "C" void ThorBatteryStaticInit();
+extern "C" void thor_wifi_power_source(void);
+using ThorGauge::Cycle;
+
+class ThorBatterySource : public IOPMPowerSource {
+    OSDeclareDefaultStructors(ThorBatterySource)
+    void clearOptional(const OSSymbol *key) {
+        if (!properties->getObject(key)) return;
+        properties->removeObject(key);
+        removeProperty(key);
+        settingsChangedSinceUpdate = true;
+    }
+public:
+    void apply(const Cycle &s) {
+        setBatteryInstalled(true);
+        setMaxCapacity(100);
+        setCurrentCapacity(s.percent());
+        if (s.has(ThorGauge::Status) && s.values[ThorGauge::Status] != 0)
+            setIsCharging(s.values[ThorGauge::Status] == 1);
+        else clearOptional(chargingKey);
+        // Thor can charge wirelessly. USB online=0 cannot establish that every
+        // charging input is absent. Charging itself proves a connected supply.
+        if ((s.has(ThorGauge::UsbOnline) && s.values[ThorGauge::UsbOnline]) ||
+            (s.has(ThorGauge::Status) && s.values[ThorGauge::Status]==1)) setExternalConnected(true);
+        else clearOptional(externalConnectedKey);
+        updateStatus();
+    }
+};
+OSDefineMetaClassAndStructors(ThorBatterySource, IOPMPowerSource)
+
+namespace {
+constexpr uint32_t smemBytes = 0x200000;
+uint32_t prepared, coldReleased;
+QcomAdspColdOwner coldOwner{};
+IOMemoryMap *coldMap;
+QcomSmem coldSmem{};
+struct Edge {
+    QcomSmem smem{};
+    QcomGlink link{};
+    QcomGlinkChannel *channel = nullptr;
+    uint8_t intents[4*1024] = {};
+    IOMemoryMap *smemMap = nullptr, *ipccMap = nullptr;
+    ThorBatterySource *battery = nullptr;
+    bool down = false;
+    Cycle cycle{};
+    uint32_t peerBits = 0, found = 0;
+    bool checkedGlink = false;
+    QcomGlinkChannel *audio = nullptr;
+    uint8_t audioIntents[20*512] = {};
+    unsigned audioPackets = 0;
+    uint64_t audioUpAtUs = 0, audioFirstUs = 0;
+} edge;
+
+// v230: diagnostic only. Once its audio services are up, the ADSP opens
+// adsp_apps (GPR: SPF, APM, PRM) towards the AP. Listen on the same edge with
+// the channel's own intents (0x200 x 0x14 in the stock DT) and record when the
+// service appears and what it sends first. Nothing is answered, so no graph,
+// clock or DMA request is ever made.
+static uint64_t audioUs() { uint64_t ns = 0; absolutetime_to_nanoseconds(mach_absolute_time(), &ns); return ns / 1000; }
+void audioState(void *, QcomGlinkChannel *, int up) {
+    const uint64_t at = audioUs();
+    if (up && !edge.audioUpAtUs) edge.audioUpAtUs = at;
+    IOLog("THOR AUDIO V230: adsp_apps %s at_us=%llu since_up_us=%llu packets=%u\n",
+          up ? "up" : "down", (unsigned long long)at,
+          (unsigned long long)(edge.audioUpAtUs ? at - edge.audioUpAtUs : 0), edge.audioPackets);
+}
+void audioReceive(void *, QcomGlinkChannel *, const uint8_t *p, uint32_t bytes) {
+    ++edge.audioPackets;
+    if (!edge.audioFirstUs) edge.audioFirstUs = audioUs();
+    if (edge.audioPackets > 16) return;
+    char hex[3 * 32 + 1] = "";
+    unsigned n = 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < bytes && i < 32; ++i) n += snprintf(hex + n, sizeof hex - n, "%02x", p[i]);
+    IOLog("THOR AUDIO V230: packet=%u bytes=%u since_up_us=%llu data=%s\n", edge.audioPackets, bytes,
+          (unsigned long long)(audioUs() - edge.audioUpAtUs), hex);
+}
+
+IOMemoryMap *map(uint64_t pa, uint32_t bytes) {
+    IODeviceMemory *mem = IODeviceMemory::withRange(pa, bytes);
+    if (!mem) return nullptr;
+    auto result = mem->map(kIOMapAnywhere | kIOMapInhibitCache);
+    mem->release();
+    return result;
+}
+bool item(const QcomSmemPartition &p, uint16_t id, uint32_t &offset, uint32_t &bytes) {
+    if (qcom_smem_find_stable(&edge.smem, &p, id, &offset, &bytes)) return false;
+    return !(offset & 3) && offset >= p.offset && offset < smemBytes &&
+        bytes <= smemBytes-offset && offset-p.offset <= p.size && bytes <= p.size-(offset-p.offset);
+}
+bool inbound(const QcomSmemPartition &p) {
+    uint32_t at, bytes;
+    if (!item(p,443,at,bytes) || bytes < 20) return false;
+    QcomSmp2p peer{};
+    peer.in = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(edge.smem.base + at);
+    if (qcom_smp2p_check_in(peer.in,0,2) || (peer.in[3] & 0xffffu) > (bytes-20)/20) return false;
+    const int idx = qcom_smp2p_find_in(&peer,"slave-kernel");
+    if (idx < 0) return false;
+    edge.peerBits = qcom_smp2p_in_value(&peer,idx);
+    return (edge.peerBits & 0x8b) == 2; // READY and no fatal/stop/shutdown ACK
+}
+void doorbell(void *) {
+    auto regs = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(edge.ipccMap->getVirtualAddress());
+    regs[QCOM_IPCC_SEND/4] = qcom_ipcc_id(QCOM_IPCC_CLIENT_LPASS,QCOM_IPCC_SIGNAL_GLINK_QMP);
+    __asm__ volatile("dsb oshst" ::: "memory");
+}
+void state(void *, QcomGlinkChannel *, int up) { if (!up) edge.down = true; }
+void receive(void *, QcomGlinkChannel *, const uint8_t *p, uint32_t bytes) { edge.cycle.answer(p,bytes); }
+
+bool firstFrame(uint32_t descAt, uint32_t rxAt, uint32_t rxBytes) {
+    volatile uint32_t *words = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(edge.smem.base+descAt);
+    const uint32_t d[4] = {words[0],words[1],words[2],words[3]};
+    __asm__ volatile("dmb oshld" ::: "memory");
+    return ThorGauge::initialVersion(d,0x4000,rxBytes,qcom_smem_read32(&edge.smem,rxAt));
+}
+// The descriptor and inbound FIFO are established by the ready peer on
+// some boots. The outbound 16 KiB FIFO is AP-owned. Allocate only when the
+// remote has actually offered a fresh VERSION and no AP indices are in use.
+bool ensureTx(const QcomSmemPartition &p, uint32_t descAt, uint32_t rxAt, uint32_t &txAt) {
+    IOMemoryMap *lockMap = map(0x1f43000,0x1000); // Thor TCSR mutex 3
+    if (!lockMap) return false;
+    auto mutex = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(lockMap->getVirtualAddress());
+    uint32_t bytes = 0;
+    bool ok = false;
+    if (pong_smem_lock(mutex)) {
+        QcomSmemPartition locked{};
+        uint32_t desc = 0, rx = 0, descBytes = 0, rxBytes = 0;
+        const bool same = !qcom_smem_partition(&edge.smem,0,2,&locked) &&
+            locked.offset == p.offset && locked.size == p.size && inbound(locked) &&
+            item(locked,478,desc,descBytes) && desc == descAt && descBytes >= 16 &&
+            item(locked,480,rx,rxBytes) && rx == rxAt && rxBytes == 0x4000 &&
+            firstFrame(desc,rx,rxBytes);
+        if (same) {
+            int rc = qcom_smem_find_stable(&edge.smem,&locked,479,&txAt,&bytes);
+            if (rc == QcomSmemMissing)
+                rc = qcom_smem_alloc(&edge.smem,&locked,479,0x4000);
+            if (!rc || rc == QcomSmemExists)
+                ok = item(locked,479,txAt,bytes) && bytes == 0x4000;
+        }
+        pong_smem_unlock(mutex);
+    }
+    lockMap->release();
+    return ok;
+}
+bool connect(const QcomSmemPartition &p) {
+    uint32_t pos[3] = {}, bytes[3] = {};
+    edge.checkedGlink = true;
+    edge.found = 0;
+    for (unsigned i=0; i<3; ++i)
+        if (item(p,uint16_t(478+i),pos[i],bytes[i])) edge.found |= 1u << i;
+    uint32_t preparation=__atomic_load_n(&prepared,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE);
+    if (preparation==1) return false;
+    const bool owned = preparation==2;
+    if (owned) {
+        if (!__atomic_load_n(&coldReleased,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE) ||
+            (edge.found & 3)!=3 || pos[0]!=coldOwner.items[1] || pos[1]!=coldOwner.items[2] ||
+            qcom_smem_adsp_edge_state(&coldSmem,&coldOwner)!=1 || bytes[0]!=32 ||
+            bytes[1]!=0x4000 || ((edge.found&4) && bytes[2]!=0x4000)) return false;
+        volatile uint32_t *cur=reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(edge.smem.base+pos[0]);
+        if (cur[0] || cur[1] || cur[2] || cur[3]>=0x4000 || (cur[3]&7)) return false;
+    } else {
+        if ((edge.found & 5) != 5 || bytes[0] < 16 || bytes[2]!=0x4000 ||
+            !firstFrame(pos[0],pos[2],bytes[2])) return false;
+        if (!(edge.found & 2)) {
+            if (!ensureTx(p,pos[0],pos[2],pos[1])) return false;
+            bytes[1] = 0x4000;
+            edge.found |= 2;
+        }
+        if (bytes[1]!=0x4000 || !firstFrame(pos[0],pos[2],bytes[2])) return false;
+    }
+    edge.ipccMap = map(0xed18000,0x1000);
+    if (!edge.ipccMap) return false;
+    auto desc = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(edge.smem.base + pos[0]);
+    QcomGlinkFifo tx{desc+1,desc,edge.smem.base+pos[1],bytes[1]};
+    QcomGlinkFifo rx{desc+3,desc+2,(edge.found&4) ? edge.smem.base+pos[2] : nullptr,bytes[2]};
+    qcom_glink_init(&edge.link,tx,rx,doorbell,nullptr);
+    const QcomGlinkClient client{state,receive};
+    edge.channel = qcom_glink_channel(&edge.link,"PMIC_RTR_ADSP_APPS",1024,4,edge.intents,&client,nullptr,0);
+    if (!edge.channel) return false;
+    static const QcomGlinkClient audioClient{audioState,audioReceive};
+    edge.audio = qcom_glink_channel(&edge.link,"adsp_apps",512,20,edge.audioIntents,&audioClient,nullptr,0);
+    IOLog("THOR AUDIO V230: adsp_apps listener %s\n", edge.audio ? "armed" : "unavailable");
+    return true;
+}
+bool startClass() {
+    void *module = OSMetaClass::preModLoad(g_kernel_kmod_info.name);
+    if (!module) return false;
+    ThorBatteryStaticInit();
+    return OSMetaClass::postModLoad(module) == 0;
+}
+void withdraw() {
+    if (!edge.battery) return;
+    edge.battery->terminate();
+    edge.battery->release();
+    edge.battery = nullptr;
+}
+bool publish() {
+    if (!edge.cycle.measured()) { withdraw(); return false; }
+    const bool first = !edge.battery;
+    if (first) {
+        static bool initialized, ready;
+        if (!initialized) { ready = startClass(); initialized = true; }
+        if (!ready) return false;
+        auto *b = OSTypeAlloc(ThorBatterySource);
+        auto *provider = IOService::getPlatform();
+        if (!b || !provider || !b->init() || !b->attach(provider)) {
+            if (b) b->release();
+            return false;
+        }
+        edge.battery = b;
+        b->setName("ThorBattery");
+    }
+    edge.battery->apply(edge.cycle);
+    if (first) {
+        edge.battery->registerService();
+        IOLog("THOR BATTERY V226: published source=pmic-glink percent=%u\n",edge.cycle.percent());
+        thor_wifi_power_source();   // v240: wifid starts after this
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+void runSession() {
+    edge.smemMap = map(0x80900000,smemBytes);
+    if (!edge.smemMap) { IOLog("THOR BATTERY V226: no SMEM mapping\n"); return; }
+    edge.smem = {reinterpret_cast<volatile uint8_t *>(edge.smemMap->getVirtualAddress()),smemBytes};
+    QcomSmemPartition p{};
+    bool connected = false;
+    int partition = 0;
+    for (unsigned i=0; i<31 && !connected; ++i) {
+        partition = qcom_smem_partition(&edge.smem,0,2,&p);
+        if (!partition && inbound(p)) connected = connect(p);
+        if (!connected && i!=30) IOSleep(1000);
+    }
+    IOLog("THOR BATTERY V226: edge=%u partition=%d slave=%#x glink_checked=%u glink_items=%#x\n",
+          unsigned(connected),partition,edge.peerBits,unsigned(edge.checkedGlink),edge.found);
+    const char *reason = "no-adsp-edge";
+    unsigned idle = 0, disabled = 0;
+    // No transaction ID in this PMIC protocol. After a timeout, close the
+    // session on a mandatory timeout. Retire an unanswered optional field for
+    // this channel lifetime: its distinct opcode/property can never match again.
+    while (connected && !edge.down && inbound(p)) {
+        if (!edge.link.rx.data) {
+            uint32_t rx,bytes;
+            if (item(p,480,rx,bytes)) {
+                if (bytes!=0x4000) { reason="invalid-rx-size"; break; }
+                qcom_glink_set_rx(&edge.link,edge.smem.base+rx,bytes);
+            }
+        }
+        if (qcom_glink_poll(&edge.link)<0) { reason="invalid-frame"; break; }
+        if (edge.down) { reason="channel-closed"; break; }
+        edge.cycle.skipDisabled(disabled);
+        if (edge.channel->up && edge.cycle.cursor == ThorGauge::FieldCount) {
+            publish();
+            edge.cycle = {};
+            idle = 0;
+            // Keep servicing the link between publishes: the ADSP's open request
+            // and GPR packets arrive on this edge at any time.
+            bool alive = true;
+            for (unsigned k = 0; k < 100 && alive && inbound(p); ++k) {
+                if (qcom_glink_poll(&edge.link) < 0 || edge.down) alive = false;
+                else IOSleep(100);
+            }
+            if (!alive) { reason = edge.down ? "channel-closed" : "invalid-frame"; break; }
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (edge.channel->up && !edge.cycle.sent) {
+            uint32_t request[6];
+            edge.cycle.request(request);
+            if (qcom_glink_send(&edge.link,edge.channel,request,sizeof(request)) == QcomGlinkOk) {
+                edge.cycle.sent = true;
+                idle = 0;
+            }
+        }
+        if (++idle >= 150) {
+            if (edge.channel->up && edge.cycle.retireOptional(disabled)) { idle=0; continue; }
+            reason="peer-timeout";
+            break;
+        }
+        IOSleep(20);
+    }
+    withdraw();
+    IOLog("THOR BATTERY V226: stop=%s peer=%#x published=0\n",reason,edge.peerBits);
+    OSSafeReleaseNULL(edge.ipccMap);
+    OSSafeReleaseNULL(edge.smemMap);
+}
+uint32_t generations, running;
+void startWorker();
+void worker(void *,wait_result_t) {
+    unsigned generation=__atomic_load_n(&generations,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE);
+    runSession();
+    bzero(&edge,sizeof(edge));
+    __atomic_store_n(&running,0,__ATOMIC_RELEASE);
+    if (__atomic_load_n(&generations,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)!=generation) startWorker();
+}
+void startWorker() {
+    uint32_t expected=0;
+    if (!__atomic_compare_exchange_n(&running,&expected,1,false,__ATOMIC_ACQ_REL,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)) return;
+    thread_t thread=nullptr;
+    if (kernel_thread_start(worker,nullptr,&thread)==KERN_SUCCESS) thread_deallocate(thread);
+    else { __atomic_store_n(&running,0,__ATOMIC_RELEASE); IOLog("THOR BATTERY V226: worker unavailable\n"); }
+}
+void requestWorker() {
+    __atomic_add_fetch(&generations,1,__ATOMIC_ACQ_REL);
+    startWorker();
+}
+}
+extern "C" void thor_battery_start() {
+    static uint32_t once;
+    if (__atomic_exchange_n(&once,1,__ATOMIC_ACQ_REL)) return;
+    char board[16]={};
+    if (PE_parse_boot_argn("arp0",board,sizeof(board)) && !strcmp(board,"thor")) requestWorker();
+}
+extern "C" int pong_thor_adsp_prepare_cold() {
+    uint32_t expected=0;
+    if (!__atomic_compare_exchange_n(&prepared,&expected,1,false,__ATOMIC_ACQ_REL,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)) return -1;
+    int rc=QcomSmemBadPartition;
+    coldMap=map(0x80900000,smemBytes);
+    IOMemoryMap *lockMap=map(0x1f43000,0x1000);
+    if (coldMap && lockMap) {
+        coldSmem={reinterpret_cast<volatile uint8_t *>(coldMap->getVirtualAddress()),smemBytes};
+        auto mutex=reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(lockMap->getVirtualAddress());
+        if (pong_smem_lock(mutex)) {
+            rc=qcom_smem_adsp_prepare_cold(&coldSmem,&coldOwner);
+            if (!rc) rc=qcom_smem_adsp_edge_state(&coldSmem,&coldOwner);
+            pong_smem_unlock(mutex);
+        }
+    }
+    OSSafeReleaseNULL(lockMap);
+    if (rc) OSSafeReleaseNULL(coldMap);
+    __atomic_store_n(&prepared,rc ? 3u : 2u,__ATOMIC_RELEASE);
+    IOLog("THOR ADSP EDGE V227: present=%#x blocker=%u sizes=%u/%u/%u/%u/%u\n",
+          coldOwner.present,coldOwner.blocker,coldOwner.sizes[0],coldOwner.sizes[1],
+          coldOwner.sizes[2],coldOwner.sizes[3],coldOwner.sizes[4]);
+    IOLog("THOR BATTERY V226: prepared-cold-edge=%d\n",rc);
+    return rc;
+}
+extern "C" int pong_thor_adsp_edge_state() {
+    if (__atomic_load_n(&prepared,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)!=2) return QcomSmemInvalidSignal;
+    return qcom_smem_adsp_edge_state(&coldSmem,&coldOwner);
+}
+extern "C" bool pong_thor_adsp_proxy_handover() {
+    return __atomic_load_n(&prepared,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE)==2 && qcom_smem_adsp_handover(&coldSmem,&coldOwner);
+}
+extern "C" void pong_thor_adsp_ready_notify() {
+    if (pong_thor_adsp_edge_state()!=1) return;
+    __atomic_store_n(&coldReleased,1,__ATOMIC_RELEASE);
+    requestWorker();
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemAoss.h b/ThorModemAoss.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3058e0440b175083a0b34a8dfe363c1f12e231ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemAoss.h
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include "QcomQmp.h"
+
+/* Same shared RAM descriptor and AP send bounds as PoNG QcomQmp.c. A
+ * stable snapshot describes the link; a channel owner still has to
+ * establish and serialize the handshake before sending any messages. */
+constexpr uint32_t kThorAossRamBytes = 0x400;
+constexpr uint32_t kThorAossUp = 0x0000ffff;
+struct ThorAossSnapshot {
+    uint32_t words[15];
+};
+
+struct ThorAossStatus {
+    const char *state;
+    uint32_t version;
+    uint32_t box;
+    uint32_t boxBytes;
+    uint32_t aopUp;
+    uint32_t appsUp;
+};
+
+static ThorAossStatus thorAossStatus(const ThorAossSnapshot &first, const ThorAossSnapshot &second)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 15; ++i) {
+        if (first.words[i] != second.words[i]) {
+            return {"unstable", 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
+        }
+    }
+
+    const auto *r = second.words;
+    ThorAossStatus info{"bad-magic", r[1], r[14], r[13], 0, 0};
+    if (r[0] != 0x4d41494c) {
+        return info;
+    }
+    if (info.version != 1) {
+        info.state = "bad-version";
+        return info;
+    }
+    if ((info.box & 3u) || info.box < sizeof(ThorAossSnapshot) ||
+        info.box > kThorAossRamBytes || info.boxBytes > kThorAossRamBytes - info.box ||
+        info.boxBytes < QCOM_QMP_MESSAGE + sizeof(uint32_t)) {
+        info.state = "bad-ap-box";
+        return info;
+    }
+
+    // Each mask contains link, link ACK, channel and channel ACK, in that order.
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
+        info.aopUp |= uint32_t(r[3 + i] == kThorAossUp) << i;
+        info.appsUp |= uint32_t(r[9 + i] == kThorAossUp) << i;
+    }
+    // qcom_qmp_step adopts an existing channel with these five UP signals.
+    info.state = info.appsUp == 0xf && (info.aopUp & 4) ? "open-observed" :
+        (info.aopUp || info.appsUp) ? "handshake-pending" : "inactive";
+    return info;
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemAossChannel.h b/ThorModemAossChannel.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..873d217861c0ee607eb9d293c4ba3e11c6143fc9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemAossChannel.h
@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ThorModemAoss.h"
+
+constexpr unsigned kThorAossAopChannelAck = 6;
+constexpr unsigned kThorAossApChannel = 11;
+constexpr unsigned kThorAossApChannelAck = 12;
+
+struct ThorAossChannelResult {
+    const char *state;
+    uint32_t apChannel;
+    uint32_t apAck;
+    bool freshAck = false;
+};
+
+static bool thorAossClosed(uint32_t state)
+{
+    return state == 0 || state == 0xffff0000;
+}
+
+// AP channel and peer acknowledgement are the only fields that may change.
+static bool thorAossSameChannel(const ThorAossSnapshot &initial, const ThorAossSnapshot &next)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(initial.words) / sizeof(initial.words[0]); ++i) {
+        if (i != kThorAossApChannel && i != kThorAossApChannelAck &&
+            next.words[i] != initial.words[i]) {
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+template <typename Read, typename Write, typename Kick, typename Wait>
+static ThorAossChannelResult thorAossOpenChannel(Read read, Write write, Kick kick, Wait wait)
+{
+    ThorAossSnapshot initial{};
+    if (!read(initial)) {
+        return {"unstable", 0, 0};
+    }
+    const auto status = thorAossStatus(initial, initial);
+    const uint32_t originalChannel = initial.words[kThorAossApChannel];
+    const uint32_t originalAck = initial.words[kThorAossApChannelAck];
+    if (status.version != 1 || status.box != 0x128 || status.boxBytes != 0x2d8 ||
+        status.aopUp != 0xf) {
+        return {"descriptor-not-admitted", originalChannel, originalAck};
+    }
+    if (status.appsUp == 0xf) {
+        return {"existing-open", originalChannel, originalAck};
+    }
+    if (status.appsUp != 0x3 || !thorAossClosed(originalChannel) ||
+        !thorAossClosed(originalAck)) {
+        return {"state-not-admitted", originalChannel, originalAck};
+    }
+
+    // Complete the already-acknowledged link using the vendor channel order.
+    // The AP owns D_MCORE_CH and D_UCORE_CH_ACK. The AOP owns D_MCORE_CH_ACK.
+    write(kThorAossApChannel, kThorAossUp);
+    kick();
+    ThorAossSnapshot current{};
+    bool acknowledgedAop = false;
+    do {
+        if (!read(current)) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        const uint32_t channel = current.words[kThorAossApChannel];
+        const uint32_t ack = current.words[kThorAossApChannelAck];
+        if (!thorAossSameChannel(initial, current) || channel != kThorAossUp ||
+            (ack != kThorAossUp && !thorAossClosed(ack))) {
+            return {"peer-state-changed", channel, ack};
+        }
+        if (!acknowledgedAop) {
+            write(kThorAossAopChannelAck, kThorAossUp);
+            kick();
+            acknowledgedAop = true;
+        }
+        if (ack == kThorAossUp) {
+            return {"open-acked", channel, ack, true};
+        }
+    } while (wait());
+
+    // Verify ownership and identity again before undoing our sole changed
+    // word. Never reset the inherited AP link or write the AOP's ACK.
+    if (!read(current) || !thorAossSameChannel(initial, current) ||
+        current.words[kThorAossApChannel] != kThorAossUp) {
+        return {"rollback-not-admitted", current.words[kThorAossApChannel],
+            current.words[kThorAossApChannelAck]};
+    }
+    const uint32_t ack = current.words[kThorAossApChannelAck];
+    if (ack == kThorAossUp) {
+        return {acknowledgedAop ? "open-acked-at-deadline" : "peer-ack-unadopted", kThorAossUp, ack, acknowledgedAop};
+    }
+    if (!thorAossClosed(ack)) {
+        return {"rollback-not-admitted", kThorAossUp, ack};
+    }
+    write(kThorAossApChannel, originalChannel);
+    kick();
+    ThorAossSnapshot rolledBack{};
+    if (!read(rolledBack) || !thorAossSameChannel(initial, rolledBack) ||
+        rolledBack.words[kThorAossApChannel] != originalChannel ||
+        !thorAossClosed(rolledBack.words[kThorAossApChannelAck])) {
+        return {"rollback-unverified", rolledBack.words[kThorAossApChannel],
+            rolledBack.words[kThorAossApChannelAck]};
+    }
+    return {"timeout-rolled-back", rolledBack.words[kThorAossApChannel],
+        rolledBack.words[kThorAossApChannelAck]};
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemAossPacket.h b/ThorModemAossPacket.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3c0c04e3446b13fd225e4db3fee9fba34bccc681
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemAossPacket.h
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ThorModemAoss.h"
+
+template <typename Read>
+static bool thorAossMailboxOpen(Read read)
+{
+    ThorAossSnapshot a{}, b{};
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 15; ++i) a.words[i] = read(i);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 15; ++i) b.words[i] = read(i);
+    const auto status = thorAossStatus(a, b);
+    return status.aopUp == 0xf && status.appsUp == 0xf && status.box == 0x128 && status.boxBytes == 0x2d8;
+}
+
+// Publish the complete padded packet before the length and the doorbell. A
+// timeout keeps its length intact so a second sender cannot steal ownership.
+template <unsigned Bytes, typename Read, typename Write, typename Kick, typename Wait>
+static const char *thorAossSend(const char (&packet)[Bytes], Read read, Write write,
+                                Kick kick, Wait wait, bool &published)
+{
+    static_assert(Bytes && !(Bytes % 4) && Bytes <= 0x2d8 - 4, "mailbox bounds");
+    published = false;
+    constexpr unsigned box = 0x128 / 4;
+    if (!thorAossMailboxOpen(read)) return "channel-unavailable";
+    if (read(box)) return "mailbox-busy";
+    for (unsigned offset = 0; offset < Bytes; offset += 4) {
+        uint32_t word = 0;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
+            word |= static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<uint8_t>(packet[offset + i])) << (i * 8);
+        write(box + 1 + offset / 4, word);
+    }
+    write(box, Bytes);
+    published = true;
+    const uint32_t readback = read(box);
+    if (readback != Bytes && readback != 0) return "publication-changed";
+    kick();
+    // A zero already present at readback cannot independently establish that
+    // the peer retired this publication. Do not retry an ambiguous request.
+    if (!readback) return "cleared-before-doorbell";
+    do {
+        if (!thorAossMailboxOpen(read)) return "channel-changed";
+        const uint32_t length = read(box);
+        if (!length) return nullptr;
+        if (length != Bytes) return "mailbox-changed";
+    } while (wait());
+    return "ack-timeout";
+}
+
+// Linux soc_sleep_stats uses a 36-byte aligned packet, while the Cape
+// remoteproc driver sends the full 64-byte zero-padded qmp_name=modem packet.
+static constexpr char kThorDdrPacket[36] = "{class: ddr, res: drvs_ddr_votes}";
+static constexpr char kThorModemOnPacket[64] = "{class: image, res: load_state, name: modem, val: on}";
+
+enum ThorAossPrerequisite : unsigned {
+    kThorMssMetadata = 1,
+    kThorMssChannel = 2,
+};
+
+// The verified firmware and channel/SMEM preflight complete on independent
+// workers. Only the transition that supplies the last prerequisite can send.
+static bool thorModemMayRequest(unsigned &state, ThorAossPrerequisite event)
+{
+    const unsigned previous = __atomic_fetch_or(&state, unsigned(event), __ATOMIC_ACQ_REL);
+    return previous != (kThorMssMetadata | kThorMssChannel) &&
+           (previous | unsigned(event)) == (kThorMssMetadata | kThorMssChannel);
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemArc.h b/ThorModemArc.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a67d7787b23b0cf75d12b37106fb98e0849f0761
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemArc.h
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ThorModemCmdDb.h"
+
+// This board's three ACTIVE ARC votes share one APSS DRV. powerLock protects
+// both TCS4 MMIO and the values below, including GPU writes before preflight.
+struct ThorModemArc {
+    struct Vote {
+        uint32_t address;
+        uint32_t ack;
+        // Combined boot-lifetime minimum. The legacy API has no owner
+        // token that could release another consumer's inherited vote.
+        uint32_t retainedFloor;
+        bool known;
+    };
+    static constexpr unsigned railCount = 3;
+    static constexpr unsigned allRetained = (1u << railCount) - 1;
+    Vote votes[railCount] = {{0x30000, 0, 0, false}, {0x30060, 0, 0, false},
+                             {0x300b0, 0, 0, false}};
+    // Wi-Fi observes the shared MXA vote. The modem has no floor on it.
+    Vote sharedMx{0x30010, 0, 0, false};
+
+    Vote *find(uint32_t address) {
+        for (auto &v : votes) if (v.address == address) return &v;
+        return address == sharedMx.address ? &sharedMx : nullptr;
+    }
+
+    unsigned retainedMask() const {
+        unsigned mask = 0;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < railCount; ++i) {
+            const Vote &v = votes[i];
+            if (v.known && v.retainedFloor && v.ack >= v.retainedFloor)
+                mask |= 1u << i;
+        }
+        return mask;
+    }
+
+    template <class Write>
+    bool legacy(uint32_t address, uint32_t value, Write write) {
+        Vote *v = find(address);
+        if (!v) return write(address, value);
+        const uint32_t effective = value < v->retainedFloor ? v->retainedFloor : value;
+        const bool ok = write(address, effective);
+        v->known = ok;
+        if (ok) v->ack = effective;
+        return ok;
+    }
+
+    struct Result {
+        const char *state;
+        unsigned inherited, sent, acknowledged;
+        uint32_t level[railCount];
+    };
+
+    // Admission is checked for every rail before publishing any floor.
+    // Never lower a firmware-inherited vote of unknown value. The highest
+    // legal index in the runtime AUX table is the only safe initial request
+    // in that case; fail closed if another board has further performance levels.
+    template <class Write>
+    Result acquire(const ThorModemCmdDb &db, Write write) {
+        Result r{"invalid-cmd-db", 0, 0, 0, {}};
+        const ThorModemRail rails[railCount] = {db.cx, db.mss, db.xo};
+        if (db.version != 1 || db.xo.corner != 3) return r;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < railCount; ++i) {
+            const auto &rail = rails[i];
+            const auto &vote = votes[i];
+            if (rail.address != vote.address || rail.corner <= 0 ||
+                rail.highest < rail.corner || rail.highest > 15 ||
+                (vote.known && vote.ack > unsigned(rail.highest))) return r;
+            if (!vote.known && rail.corner != rail.highest) {
+                r.state = "baseline-unknown";
+                return r;
+            }
+            r.level[i] = unsigned(rail.corner);
+            if (vote.known && vote.ack >= r.level[i]) {
+                r.inherited |= 1u << i;
+                r.level[i] = vote.ack;
+            }
+        }
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < railCount; ++i) {
+            Vote &v = votes[i];
+            v.retainedFloor = r.level[i];
+            if (!(r.inherited & (1u << i))) {
+                r.sent |= 1u << i;
+                if (!legacy(v.address, v.retainedFloor, write)) {
+                    // An ambiguous late completion is possible; keep this
+                    // startup floor as well as earlier acknowledged votes.
+                    r.state = "vote-failed";
+                    return r;
+                }
+            }
+            r.acknowledged |= 1u << i;
+        }
+        r.state = "held";
+        return r;
+    }
+};
diff --git a/ThorModemCmdDb.h b/ThorModemCmdDb.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..76d9381e1ddb663a8e4789a28db9d39282b01f80
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemCmdDb.h
@@ -0,0 +1,217 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent */
+#pragma once
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+/* Read-only CMD DB v1 layout, also used by PongAdrenoPower.c. Keep the
+ * modem lookup independent of the GPU-only requirements and HFI tables. */
+struct ThorModemRail {
+    uint32_t address;
+    int corner, highest;
+};
+struct ThorModemCmdDb {
+    uint32_t version;
+    ThorModemRail cx, mss, xo;
+};
+enum ThorModemCmdStatus {
+    kThorCmdOk,
+    kThorCmdInvalid,
+    kThorCmdDuplicate,
+    kThorCmdMissing,
+    kThorCmdCornerMissing,
+};
+static constexpr size_t kThorCmdDbBytes = 0x20000;
+
+static uint16_t thorCmdLe16(const uint8_t *p)
+{
+    return uint16_t(p[0]) | uint16_t(uint16_t(p[1]) << 8);
+}
+
+static uint32_t thorCmdLe32(const uint8_t *p)
+{
+    return uint32_t(thorCmdLe16(p)) | (uint32_t(thorCmdLe16(p + 2)) << 16);
+}
+
+static int thorCmdCorner(const uint8_t *p, size_t bytes, uint16_t nominal, int &highest)
+{
+    highest = -1;
+    if (!bytes || (bytes & 1) || bytes > 512 || thorCmdLe16(p)) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    uint16_t previous = 0;
+    int corner = -1;
+    bool padding = false;
+    for (size_t index = 1; index < bytes / 2; ++index) {
+        const uint16_t level = thorCmdLe16(p + 2 * index);
+        if (!level) {
+            padding = true;
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (padding || level < previous) {
+            return -1;
+        }
+        previous = level;
+        highest = static_cast<int>(index);
+        if (corner < 0 && level >= nominal) {
+            corner = static_cast<int>(index);
+        }
+    }
+    return corner;
+}
+
+struct ThorCmdTable { size_t start, end, aux; unsigned slave; };
+struct ThorCmdDirectory {
+    ThorCmdTable tables[8];
+    unsigned count;
+};
+static constexpr size_t kThorCmdEntryBytes = 24;
+
+static bool thorCmdDirectory(const uint8_t *db, size_t bytes, ThorCmdDirectory &directory)
+{
+    constexpr size_t payload = 144, rowBytes = 16;
+    if (!db || bytes != kThorCmdDbBytes || !thorCmdLe32(db) || thorCmdLe32(db + 4) != 0x0c0330db) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    directory.count = 0;
+    for (auto &table : directory.tables) {
+        const uint8_t *row = db + 8 + rowBytes * directory.count;
+        const unsigned slave = thorCmdLe16(row);
+        if (!slave) {
+            break;
+        }
+        const size_t start = payload + thorCmdLe16(row + 2);
+        const size_t size = kThorCmdEntryBytes * thorCmdLe16(row + 6);
+        const size_t aux = payload + thorCmdLe16(row + 4);
+        if (start > bytes || size > bytes - start || aux > bytes) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        table = {start, start + size, aux, slave};
+        ++directory.count;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+struct ThorCmdRailSpec {
+    char name[8];
+    uint16_t level;
+    bool allowAbsentCorner;
+};
+template <size_t N>
+static ThorModemCmdStatus thorCmdReadRails(const uint8_t *db, size_t bytes,
+        const ThorCmdRailSpec (&specs)[N], ThorModemRail (&rails)[N])
+{
+    ThorCmdDirectory directory{};
+    if (!thorCmdDirectory(db, bytes, directory)) {
+        return kThorCmdInvalid;
+    }
+    const auto &tables = directory.tables;
+    const unsigned count = directory.count;
+    static_assert(N > 0 && N < 32, "rail mask size");
+    unsigned seen = 0;
+    for (unsigned index = 0; index < count; ++index) {
+        const auto &table = tables[index];
+        for (size_t offset = table.start; offset < table.end; offset += kThorCmdEntryBytes) {
+            const uint8_t *entry = db + offset;
+            for (unsigned rail = 0; rail < N; ++rail) {
+                if (memcmp(entry, specs[rail].name, sizeof(specs[rail].name))) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (seen & (1U << rail)) {
+                    return kThorCmdDuplicate;
+                }
+                const uint32_t address = thorCmdLe32(entry + 16);
+                const size_t size = thorCmdLe16(entry + 20);
+                const size_t start = table.aux + thorCmdLe16(entry + 22);
+                if (!address || (address & 3) || table.slave != 3 || ((address >> 16) & 7) != table.slave ||
+                    start > bytes || size > bytes - start) {
+                    return kThorCmdInvalid;
+                }
+                for (unsigned other = 0; size && other < count; ++other) {
+                    if (start < tables[other].end && tables[other].start < start + size) {
+                        return kThorCmdInvalid;
+                    }
+                }
+                int highest = -1;
+                const int corner = thorCmdCorner(db + start, size, specs[rail].level, highest);
+                if (!specs[rail].allowAbsentCorner && corner < 0) {
+                    return kThorCmdCornerMissing;
+                }
+                rails[rail] = {address, corner, highest};
+                seen |= 1U << rail;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    if (seen != (1U << N) - 1) return kThorCmdMissing;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < N; ++i)
+        for (unsigned j = 0; j < i; ++j)
+            if (rails[i].address == rails[j].address) return kThorCmdDuplicate;
+    return kThorCmdOk;
+}
+
+static ThorModemCmdStatus thorModemCmdDbRead(const uint8_t *db, size_t bytes, ThorModemCmdDb &out)
+{
+    // Cape's proxy domains request level 384. XO on is level 128.
+    const ThorCmdRailSpec spec[] = {{"cx.lvl", 384, false}, {"mss.lvl", 384, false}, {"xo.lvl", 128, true}};
+    ThorModemRail rails[3]{};
+    const auto status = thorCmdReadRails(db, bytes, spec, rails);
+    if (status == kThorCmdOk) out = {thorCmdLe32(db), rails[0], rails[1], rails[2]};
+    return status;
+}
+
+// HLOS voter paths in the Thor live FDT and Qualcomm waipio.c. Both paths end
+// at EBI. The four bridge/source BCMs are unique to crypto_ddr.
+static constexpr char kThorModemBcmNames[][8] = {"ACV", "MC0", "CE0", "SN3", "SN0", "SH0"};
+static constexpr unsigned kThorRprocDdrMask = 0x03, kThorCryptoDdrMask = 0x3f;
+struct ThorModemBcm {
+    uint32_t address, unit;
+    uint16_t width;
+    uint8_t vcd;
+};
+struct ThorModemBcmPaths {
+    ThorModemBcm resources[6];
+    unsigned present;
+};
+
+static ThorModemCmdStatus thorModemReadBcmPaths(const uint8_t *db, size_t bytes, ThorModemBcmPaths &out)
+{
+    ThorCmdDirectory directory{};
+    out = {};
+    if (!thorCmdDirectory(db, bytes, directory) || thorCmdLe32(db) != 1) {
+        return kThorCmdInvalid;
+    }
+    ThorModemBcmPaths found{};
+    for (unsigned t = 0; t < directory.count; ++t) {
+        const auto &table = directory.tables[t];
+        for (size_t pos = table.start; pos < table.end; pos += kThorCmdEntryBytes) {
+            const auto *entry = db + pos;
+            for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(found.resources) / sizeof(found.resources[0]); ++i) {
+                if (memcmp(entry, kThorModemBcmNames[i], sizeof(kThorModemBcmNames[i]))) continue;
+                const unsigned bit = 1u << i;
+                if (found.present & bit) return kThorCmdDuplicate;
+                const uint32_t address = thorCmdLe32(entry + 16);
+                const size_t length = thorCmdLe16(entry + 20);
+                const size_t start = table.aux + thorCmdLe16(entry + 22);
+                // cmd-db BCM slave id 5, auxiliary layout from struct bcm_db.
+                if (table.slave != 5 || ((address >> 16) & 7) != 5 ||
+                    length < 8 || start > bytes || length > bytes - start) return kThorCmdInvalid;
+                for (unsigned k = 0; k < directory.count; ++k) {
+                    const auto &header = directory.tables[k];
+                    if (start < header.end && header.start < start + length) return kThorCmdInvalid;
+                }
+                for (const auto &other : found.resources) {
+                    if (other.address == address) return kThorCmdDuplicate;
+                }
+                const auto *aux = db + start;
+                const uint32_t unit = thorCmdLe32(aux);
+                const uint16_t width = thorCmdLe16(aux + 4);
+                // Match qcom_icc_bcm_init on stock, including zero divisors.
+                found.resources[i] = {address, unit ? unit : 1u,
+                                      static_cast<uint16_t>(width ? width : 1u), aux[6]};
+                found.present |= bit;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    out = found;
+    return found.present == kThorCryptoDdrMask ? kThorCmdOk : kThorCmdMissing;
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemDdrStats.h b/ThorModemDdrStats.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0b5ada19bc2055c1fcea26f8435d9b4b179a458e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemDdrStats.h
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ThorModemAossPacket.h"
+
+// Cape soc_sleep_stats config reads the relative DDR table pointer at 0x1c.
+// Both stock mappings were observed in Recovery on physical page 0x0c3f0000.
+constexpr unsigned kThorDdrPageBase = 0x0c3f0000, kThorDdrPageBytes = 4096, kThorDdrDrivers = 18;
+constexpr uint32_t kThorDdrAbsent = 0xdeaddead, kThorDdrInvalid = 0xffffdead;
+struct ThorDdrVotes {
+    unsigned offset, modes;
+    uint32_t rows[kThorDdrDrivers];
+};
+
+template <typename Read>
+static const char *thorDdrVotes(Read read, ThorDdrVotes &out)
+{
+    const uint32_t pointer = read(0x1c / 4);
+    // The stock driver forms this address with base OR pointer. Accept either
+    // a relative offset or an address that resolves into the same mapped page.
+    const uint32_t address = kThorDdrPageBase | pointer;
+    if (address - kThorDdrPageBase >= kThorDdrPageBytes) return "offset-unavailable";
+    const uint32_t offset = address - kThorDdrPageBase;
+    constexpr unsigned header = 8, rowBytes = 16, resultBytes = 4 * kThorDdrDrivers;
+    if (offset < 0x20 || (offset & 3) || offset > kThorDdrPageBytes - header - resultBytes)
+        return "offset-unavailable";
+    const unsigned word = offset / 4;
+    if (read(word) != 0xa1157a75) return "bad-stats-magic";
+    const uint32_t modes = read(word + 1);
+    if (!modes || modes > 20 || modes * rowBytes > kThorDdrPageBytes - offset - header - resultBytes)
+        return "bad-stats-count";
+    const unsigned first = word + (header + modes * rowBytes) / 4;
+    ThorDdrVotes sample{offset, modes, {}};
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < kThorDdrDrivers; ++i) sample.rows[i] = read(first + i);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < kThorDdrDrivers; ++i)
+        if (sample.rows[i] != read(first + i)) return "unstable-votes";
+    if (read(0x1c / 4) != pointer || read(word) != 0xa1157a75 || read(word + 1) != modes)
+        return "stats-layout-changed";
+    out = sample;
+    return nullptr;
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemIcc.h b/ThorModemIcc.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..423c36d66ff57cf012a38e30bb630e7db107181e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemIcc.h
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ThorModemCmdDb.h"
+
+// Thor cape PAS requests (average=0, peak=UINT_MAX) on crypto_ddr while
+// loading and rproc_ddr during start. These are the modem contribution only:
+// an APSS active-set writer must also retain votes belonging to other clients.
+struct ThorIccCommand {
+    uint32_t address, data;
+    uint8_t resource, vcd;
+};
+
+struct ThorIccPlan {
+    ThorIccCommand commands[6];
+    unsigned count;
+    unsigned commitSlots;
+};
+
+static uint64_t thorIccDiv(uint64_t value, uint32_t divisor)
+{
+    // Downstream bcm_div rounds small nonzero demands up to one.
+    return value && value < divisor ? 1 : value / divisor;
+}
+
+static bool thorIccPlan(const ThorModemBcmPaths &paths, unsigned pathMask, ThorIccPlan &result)
+{
+    result = {};
+    if ((pathMask != kThorCryptoDdrMask && pathMask != kThorRprocDdrMask) ||
+        (paths.present & pathMask) != pathMask) return false;
+
+    // waipio HLOS BCM nodes: ebi (ACV,MC0), qxm_crypto, qnm_aggre2_noc,
+    // qns_gemnoc_sf and qns_llcc. For a peak vote only buswidth is used.
+    constexpr uint16_t busWidth[] = {4, 4, 8, 16, 16, 16};
+    constexpr uint32_t valid = 1u << 29, commit = 1u << 30;
+    ThorIccPlan plan{};
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(busWidth) / sizeof(busWidth[0]); ++i) {
+        if (!(pathMask & (1u << i))) continue;
+        const auto &bcm = paths.resources[i];
+        if (!bcm.unit || !bcm.width || (bcm.address & 3) ||
+            ((bcm.address >> 16) & 7) != 5) return false;
+        for (unsigned j = 0; j < plan.count; ++j) {
+            if (plan.commands[j].address == bcm.address) return false;
+        }
+        uint64_t peak = thorIccDiv(uint64_t(UINT32_MAX) * bcm.width, busWidth[i]);
+        peak = thorIccDiv(peak * 1000u, bcm.unit);
+        const uint32_t y = (i == 0) ? 8 : static_cast<uint32_t>(peak > 0x3fff ? 0x3fff : peak);
+        // Keep identical VCDs together. The atomic commit belongs only to
+        // the final command of each domain, including the two SN resources.
+        unsigned slot = plan.count;
+        while (slot && plan.commands[slot - 1].vcd > bcm.vcd) {
+            plan.commands[slot] = plan.commands[slot - 1];
+            --slot;
+        }
+        plan.commands[slot] = {bcm.address, valid | y, static_cast<uint8_t>(i), bcm.vcd};
+        ++plan.count;
+    }
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < plan.count; ++i) {
+        if (i + 1 == plan.count || plan.commands[i].vcd != plan.commands[i + 1].vcd) {
+            plan.commands[i].data |= commit;
+            plan.commitSlots |= 1u << i;
+        }
+    }
+    result = plan;
+    return true;
+}
diff --git a/ThorModemIccAdmission.h b/ThorModemIccAdmission.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d01bf9e7bc9984988888c767972e8f8910de7205
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorModemIccAdmission.h
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+
+#include <string.h>
+#include "ThorModemIcc.h"
+
+// Diagnostic inventory only. CMD DB describes resources; DDR statistics and
+// reusable TCS command slots are not inherited per-BCM/APSS-voter votes. This
+// version has no trusted baseline provider or owner-handoff importer, and no
+// operation here can acquire ICC ownership or permit AUTH_AND_RESET.
+enum class ThorIccDescriptionState : uint32_t { Unavailable, Rejected, Incomplete, Complete };
+enum class ThorIccDdrSampleState : uint32_t { NotObserved, Unavailable, Rejected, Stable };
+
+enum ThorIccDiagnosticSource : uint32_t {
+    kThorIccCmdDbDescription = 1u << 0,
+    kThorIccDdrStatistics = 1u << 1,
+    kThorIccTcsCommandSlots = 1u << 2, // No TCS read is added by this diagnostic.
+};
+enum ThorIccAdmissionBlocker : uint32_t {
+    kThorIccDescriptionUnavailable = 1u << 0,
+    kThorIccDescriptionRejected = 1u << 1,
+    kThorIccPlansIncomplete = 1u << 2,
+    kThorIccBaselineProviderMissing = 1u << 3,
+    kThorIccBaselineSetsIncomplete = 1u << 4,
+    kThorIccInheritedVoterUnverified = 1u << 5,
+    kThorIccOwnerHandoffMissing = 1u << 6,
+    kThorIccDiagnosticLockUnavailable = 1u << 7,
+    kThorIccDdrSampleRejected = 1u << 8,
+    kThorIccDescriptionIncomplete = 1u << 9,
+};
+
+// Fixed-size copy made under powerLock before logging. The topology fields are
+// expectations from this board, not an observed inherited-voter identity.
+struct ThorIccAdmissionSnapshot {
+    uint32_t schemaVersion = 1;
+    uint32_t diagnosticSources = 0;
+    uint32_t cmdDbVersion = 0;
+    uint32_t cmdDbStatus = kThorCmdInvalid;
+    ThorIccDescriptionState description = ThorIccDescriptionState::Unavailable;
+    ThorIccDdrSampleState ddrSample = ThorIccDdrSampleState::NotObserved;
+    uint32_t requiredResources = kThorCryptoDdrMask;
+    uint32_t describedResources = 0;
+    uint32_t requiredPlans = 3; // bit 0: rproc_ddr, bit 1: crypto_ddr
+    uint32_t validatedPlans = 0;
+    uint32_t requiredSets = 7; // bit 0: active, bit 1: wake, bit 2: sleep
+    uint32_t baselineResources[3] = {};
+    uint32_t ownerResources = 0;
+    uint32_t expectedHlosVoter = 0;
+    uint32_t expectedApssDrv = 2;
+    uint32_t inheritedVoter = UINT32_MAX;
+    uint64_t baselineEpoch = 0;
+    uint32_t baselineSources = 0;
+    uint32_t blockers = 0;
+    bool diagnosticOnly = true;
+    bool authAllowed = false;
+};
+static_assert(sizeof(ThorIccAdmissionSnapshot) <= 128, "Keep the diagnostic snapshot bounded");
+
+class ThorIccAdmissionDiagnostics {
+    uint32_t sources_ = 0, version_ = 0, status_ = kThorCmdInvalid;
+    uint32_t resources_ = 0, plans_ = 0;
+    ThorIccDescriptionState description_ = ThorIccDescriptionState::Unavailable;
+    ThorIccDdrSampleState ddr_ = ThorIccDdrSampleState::NotObserved;
+
+public:
+    // A new read replaces the prior description; partial reads never combine.
+    void clearDescriptions()
+    {
+        sources_ &= ~kThorIccCmdDbDescription;
+        version_ = resources_ = plans_ = 0;
+        status_ = kThorCmdInvalid;
+        description_ = ThorIccDescriptionState::Unavailable;
+    }
+
+    void observeDescriptions(uint32_t version, ThorModemCmdStatus status, const ThorModemBcmPaths &paths)
+    {
+        clearDescriptions();
+        sources_ |= kThorIccCmdDbDescription;
+        version_ = version;
+        status_ = status;
+        resources_ = paths.present;
+        description_ = ThorIccDescriptionState::Rejected;
+        if (version != 1 || (status != kThorCmdOk && status != kThorCmdMissing) ||
+            (paths.present & ~kThorCryptoDdrMask)) return;
+
+        ThorIccPlan plan{};
+        if (thorIccPlan(paths, kThorRprocDdrMask, plan)) plans_ |= 1;
+        if (thorIccPlan(paths, kThorCryptoDdrMask, plan)) plans_ |= 2;
+        description_ = status == kThorCmdOk && resources_ == kThorCryptoDdrMask && plans_ == 3 ?
+            ThorIccDescriptionState::Complete : ThorIccDescriptionState::Incomplete;
+    }
+
+    // Stability is only a property of the diagnostic DDR sample. No sample
+    // state changes baseline coverage, inherited voter, epoch, or ownership.
+    void observeDdrSample(ThorIccDdrSampleState state)
+    {
+        sources_ |= kThorIccDdrStatistics;
+        switch (state) {
+        case ThorIccDdrSampleState::Unavailable:
+        case ThorIccDdrSampleState::Rejected:
+        case ThorIccDdrSampleState::Stable:
+            ddr_ = state;
+            break;
+        default:
+            ddr_ = ThorIccDdrSampleState::Rejected;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
+    ThorIccAdmissionSnapshot snapshot() const
+    {
+        ThorIccAdmissionSnapshot r{};
+        r.diagnosticSources = sources_;
+        r.cmdDbVersion = version_;
+        r.cmdDbStatus = status_;
+        r.description = description_;
+        r.ddrSample = ddr_;
+        r.describedResources = resources_;
+        r.validatedPlans = plans_;
+        r.blockers = kThorIccBaselineProviderMissing | kThorIccBaselineSetsIncomplete |
+            kThorIccInheritedVoterUnverified | kThorIccOwnerHandoffMissing;
+        if (description_ == ThorIccDescriptionState::Unavailable) r.blockers |= kThorIccDescriptionUnavailable;
+        if (description_ == ThorIccDescriptionState::Rejected) r.blockers |= kThorIccDescriptionRejected;
+        if (description_ == ThorIccDescriptionState::Incomplete) r.blockers |= kThorIccDescriptionIncomplete;
+        if (plans_ != r.requiredPlans) r.blockers |= kThorIccPlansIncomplete;
+        if (ddr_ == ThorIccDdrSampleState::Rejected) r.blockers |= kThorIccDdrSampleRejected;
+        // The zero coverage/epoch, unknown inherited voter, and authAllowed=false
+        // defaults are deliberate. A future provider needs a separate reviewed
+        // protocol implementation; a diagnostic sample is never that provider.
+        return r;
+    }
+};
+
+static const char *thorIccDescriptionStateName(ThorIccDescriptionState state)
+{
+    switch (state) {
+    case ThorIccDescriptionState::Unavailable: return "unavailable";
+    case ThorIccDescriptionState::Rejected: return "rejected";
+    case ThorIccDescriptionState::Incomplete: return "incomplete";
+    case ThorIccDescriptionState::Complete: return "complete";
+    }
+    return "invalid";
+}
+
+static const char *thorIccDdrSampleStateName(ThorIccDdrSampleState state)
+{
+    switch (state) {
+    case ThorIccDdrSampleState::NotObserved: return "not-observed";
+    case ThorIccDdrSampleState::Unavailable: return "unavailable";
+    case ThorIccDdrSampleState::Rejected: return "rejected";
+    case ThorIccDdrSampleState::Stable: return "stable-diagnostic-only";
+    }
+    return "invalid";
+}
diff --git a/ThorMssChannel.h b/ThorMssChannel.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6684c15e0f3c6fd06dae40f220c2046864373477
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorMssChannel.h
@@ -0,0 +1,590 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+#pragma once
+#include "ThorMssVersion.h"
+#include "ThorQrtrProbe.h"
+#include "ThorUimStatus.h"
+#include "ThorPdLocator.h"
+
+namespace ThorMssChannel {
+enum Command : uint16_t { Open=2, Close=3, OpenAck=4, Intent=5, IntentReq=7, IntentReqAck=8, Done=6, Data=9, CloseAck=11, DataCont=12, DoneReuse=14 };
+enum class Result { Waiting, Closed, EarlyClose, Blocked, Invalid, Epoch, NoVersion, Timeout };
+constexpr uint16_t LocalId=1; // First and only channel on this cold, exclusively owned edge.
+constexpr unsigned MaxDeferred=4, MaxName=64, MaxIntents=64, MaxIntentRuns=8, MaxRefusals=4;
+// Up to three further, peer-initiated announcements within the original receive deadline.
+constexpr unsigned MaxServicePackets=3, PostReplyPackets=8;
+constexpr unsigned LocatorSlots=4;
+constexpr unsigned ServiceSlots=MaxServicePackets+PostReplyPackets+1+LocatorSlots; // Last status reply can follow the last permitted advertisement.
+constexpr unsigned BaseRecords=8+MaxDeferred+MaxIntentRuns+2*MaxRefusals+10+2*ThorQrtrProbe::MaxFragments;
+constexpr unsigned ServiceRecords=BaseRecords+MaxServicePackets*(4+ThorQrtrProbe::MaxFragments);
+constexpr unsigned QueryRecords=ServiceRecords+2; // One QMI request and one peer completion.
+constexpr unsigned MaxRecords=QueryRecords+2+(PostReplyPackets+1)*(4+ThorQrtrProbe::MaxFragments)+
+    LocatorSlots*(6+ThorQrtrProbe::MaxFragments)+4;
+struct DeferredOpen {
+    uint16_t cid{}, priority{};
+    unsigned length{};
+    char name[MaxName]{};
+};
+struct Record {
+    bool tx;
+    uint16_t cmd, cid;
+    uint32_t txHead, rxTail;
+    unsigned held{}, intentPackets{}, intentCount{};
+    uint32_t value{};
+    bool followup{}, qmi{};
+    uint8_t serviceIntent{};
+    ThorPdLocator::Transfer locator{};
+};
+struct Locator {
+    using Transfer=ThorPdLocator::Transfer;
+    bool enabled{}, published{}, forceClose{};
+    unsigned end{}, slot{}, deleteSlot{}, deleteEnd{}, deleteDone{}, acknowledged{};
+    unsigned requestMask{}, answeredMask{}, pending{}, responses{};
+    Transfer flight{};
+    uint32_t capacity[MaxIntents]{};
+    ThorPdLocator::Wire reply{};
+};
+struct Session {
+    ThorQrtrProbe::Receiver one{}, followup{}, services[ServiceSlots]{};
+    uint32_t grantTail[ServiceSlots]{};
+    bool serviceWindow{}, postReplySelected{};
+    ThorSsctlFields::Query fields{};
+    ThorUimStatus::Query uim{};
+    Locator locator{};
+    unsigned directoryMs{};
+    uint32_t localNode{ThorQrtrProbe::Broadcast};
+    uint32_t peerIntent{}, peerCapacity{}, creditFrame{}, replyEnd{};
+    unsigned replyDone{};
+    uint32_t txHead{}, rxTail{}, prevTxTail{}, prevRxHead{}, openEnd{}, ackEnd{}, closeEnd{};
+    uint16_t remoteId{}, blockedCmd{0xffff};
+    bool localAck{}, established{}, remoteClose{}, localCloseAck{}, bound{};
+    DeferredOpen deferred[MaxDeferred]{};
+    unsigned heldCount{};
+    bool sawBlockedOpen{};
+    uint16_t blockedId{}, blockedNameLength{}, blockedPriority{};
+    uint32_t blockedAvailable{};
+    uint32_t retiredIds[MaxIntents]{};
+    unsigned retiredCount{};
+    bool sawBlockedIntent{};
+    uint16_t blockedIntentCid{};
+    uint32_t blockedIntentCount{}, blockedIntentAvail{};
+    unsigned refusals{};
+    bool sawBlockedRequest{};
+    uint16_t blockedRequestCid{};
+    uint32_t blockedRequestSize{}, blockedRequestAvail{};
+    Record log[MaxRecords]{};
+    unsigned count{};
+};
+inline bool begin(Session &s,const ThorMssVersion::Session &v,ThorMssVersion::State result) {
+    if (s.bound || result!=ThorMssVersion::State::Agreed || !v.bound ||
+        !ThorMssVersion::coldOk(v.cold) || !v.offers || v.peerVersion!=1 ||
+        !v.sentAck || !v.matchingAck || v.previousTxTail!=v.txHead) return false;
+    s.txHead=v.txHead;
+    s.rxTail=v.rxTail;
+    s.prevTxTail=v.previousTxTail;
+    s.prevRxHead=v.previousRxHead;
+    s.bound=true;
+    return true;
+}
+struct Packet {
+    uint32_t word{}, param{}, body[2*MaxIntents]{};
+    uint8_t octet(unsigned i) const { return uint8_t(body[i/4]>>(8*(i%4))); }
+    bool validName() const {
+        const unsigned n=nameLength();
+        if (n<2 || n>MaxName || octet(n-1)) return false;
+        for (unsigned i=0;i+1<n;i++) if(octet(i)<33 || octet(i)>126) return false;
+        return true;
+    }
+    bool isRouter() const {
+        return nameLength()==7 && body[0]==0x52435049 && (body[1]&0x00ffffff)==0x5254;
+    }
+    bool mayRetire(const Session &s) const {
+        return s.established && (s.closeEnd || s.one.selected) && !s.remoteClose && cid()==s.remoteId &&
+               param && param<=MaxIntents-s.retiredCount;
+    }
+    bool validIntents(const Session &s) const {
+        if (!mayRetire(s)) return false;
+        for (unsigned i=0;i<param;i++) {
+            if (!body[2*i]) return false;
+            const uint32_t id=body[2*i+1];
+            for (unsigned j=0;j<s.retiredCount;j++) if (s.retiredIds[j]==id) return false;
+            for (unsigned j=0;j<i;j++) if (body[2*j+1]==id) return false;
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
+    uint32_t length{};
+    unsigned nameLength() const { return param & 0xffffu; } // OPEN encodes priority in the upper half.
+    unsigned cmd() const { return word & 0xffff; }
+    uint16_t cid() const { return uint16_t(word>>16); }
+};
+inline unsigned locatorCredit(const Session &s,unsigned bytes,unsigned excluded=MaxIntents) {
+    unsigned best=MaxIntents;
+    for(unsigned i=0;i<s.retiredCount;++i) {
+        if(i==excluded || s.retiredIds[i]==s.peerIntent || s.locator.capacity[i]<bytes) continue;
+        if(best==MaxIntents || s.locator.capacity[i]<s.locator.capacity[best]) best=i;
+    }
+    return best;
+}
+inline unsigned receiveLimit(const Session &s) {
+    if (s.uim.end && !s.uim.response) return ThorUimStatus::Capacity;
+    if(s.locator.published && !s.locator.deleteEnd) return ThorPdLocator::RxCapacity;
+    return s.fields.end && !s.fields.responseIntent ? ThorSsctlFields::ResponseCapacity : ThorQrtrProbe::Capacity;
+}
+static_assert(ThorUimStatus::Capacity+8<=sizeof(Packet::body),"fragment staging");
+static_assert(ThorUimStatus::Capacity<=sizeof(ThorQrtrProbe::Receiver::bytes),"receive staging");
+template<class Port> Packet peek(Port &p,const QcomMssGlinkSample &r,const Session &s) {
+    Packet packet{};
+    const uint32_t avail=r.cursor[3]-r.cursor[2];
+    if (avail<8) return packet;
+    const uint32_t at=r.rx_offset+r.cursor[2];
+    packet.word=p.read(at);
+    packet.param=p.read(at+4);
+    packet.length=8;
+    uint32_t payload=0;
+    if (packet.cmd()==Open && packet.nameLength()>=2 && packet.nameLength()<=MaxName)
+        payload=(packet.nameLength()+7u)&~7u;
+    else if (packet.cmd()==Intent && packet.mayRetire(s))
+        payload=packet.param*8; // Little-endian (size, ID) pairs, not a data transfer.
+    else if ((packet.cmd()==Data || packet.cmd()==DataCont) && s.one.selected) {
+        if (avail<16) { packet.length=0; return packet; }
+        const uint32_t n=p.read(at+8);
+        // For an impossible length read only the header, and reject it in step.
+        payload=8+(n<=receiveLimit(s) ? ((n+7u)&~7u) : 0);
+    }
+    if (avail<8+payload) { packet.length=0; return packet; }
+    packet.length+=payload;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i<payload/4;i++) packet.body[i]=p.read(at+8+i*4);
+    return packet;
+}
+inline bool samePacket(const Packet &a,const Packet &b) {
+    if (a.word!=b.word || a.param!=b.param || a.length!=b.length) return false;
+    for (unsigned i=0;i+8<a.length;i+=4) if (a.body[i/4]!=b.body[i/4]) return false;
+    return true;
+}
+inline bool geometry(const QcomMssGlinkSample &r,const QcomMssGlinkSample &v,const Session &s) {
+    if (!ThorMssVersion::sameLocal(r,v) || r.present!=7 || r.rx_offset!=v.rx_offset ||
+        r.size[2]!=v.size[2] || r.size[2]!=16384) return false;
+    const uint32_t tt=r.cursor[0], th=r.cursor[1], rt=r.cursor[2], rh=r.cursor[3];
+    // The VERSION exchange starts at zero and the trial has a fixed TX budget. Treat wrap or a cursor from a different epoch as terminal.
+    return !((tt|th|rt|rh)&7) && th<r.size[1] && rh<r.size[2] && tt<=th && rt<=rh &&
+           th==s.txHead && rt==s.rxTail && tt>=s.prevTxTail && rh>=s.prevRxHead;
+}
+template<class Port> Result step(Session &s,const ThorMssVersion::Session &v,Port &p) {
+    if (!s.bound) return Result::NoVersion;
+    if (!p.live()) return Result::Epoch;
+    if (!p.inTime()) return Result::Timeout;
+    QcomMssGlinkSample r{};
+    int rc=p.snapshot(r);
+    if (rc==QcomSmemUnstable) return Result::Waiting;
+    if (rc || !geometry(r,v.ring,s)) return Result::Epoch;
+    const auto tail=r.cursor[0];
+    s.prevTxTail=tail; s.prevRxHead=r.cursor[3];
+    // An OPEN_ACK counts only after the remote advanced past our OPEN.
+    // Both halves and remote consumption of our ACK must be witnessed.
+    if (!s.remoteClose && !s.established && s.localAck && s.ackEnd && tail>=s.ackEnd)
+        s.established=true;
+    if (s.localCloseAck && s.remoteClose && tail==s.txHead)
+        return p.live() ? (s.established ? Result::Closed : Result::EarlyClose) : Result::Epoch;
+
+    uint16_t tx=0, cid=0;
+    bool consume=false, defer=false, blockedOpen=false, blockedIntent=false, blockedRequest=false;
+    Packet packet{};
+    // Revoke promptly even if unrelated messages have arrived since the ACK.
+    auto &one=s.one;
+    const bool replyWindow=one.completed && one.addressedHello(s.localNode) && s.peerCapacity && !s.replyDone;
+    // A second, distinct nonreusable local buffer is available only after
+    // the peer has confirmed consumption of our HELLO using its own intent.
+    const bool next=s.followup.selected && s.replyDone;
+    auto *current=next ? &s.followup : &one;
+    unsigned localIntent=next ? ThorQrtrProbe::FollowupIntent : ThorQrtrProbe::LocalIntent;
+    // A previously verified on-peer announcement opens only the next bounded
+    // receive slot. Every slot owns a distinct, non-reusable local intent.
+    if (next && s.serviceWindow) {
+        const unsigned response=s.postReplySelected ? s.fields.responseIntent : 0;
+        const unsigned last=response ? response+PostReplyPackets+unsigned(s.uim.enabled)+(s.locator.published ? LocatorSlots : 0) :
+                            ThorQrtrProbe::FollowupIntent+MaxServicePackets;
+        // A verified QMI data response is a valid predecessor for the next
+        // control buffer. Unrelated data still terminates this directory pass.
+        for (auto &slot : s.services) {
+            if (localIntent>=last || (localIntent!=response && localIntent!=s.uim.response && !(s.locator.requestMask&(1u<<localIntent)) && !current->peerServer(s.localNode,one.word(8)))) break;
+            current=&slot;
+            ++localIntent;
+        }
+    }
+    auto &receiver=*current;
+    const bool serviceSlot=localIntent>ThorQrtrProbe::FollowupIntent;
+    const auto *server=localIntent==3 ? &s.followup :
+                       localIntent>3 ? &s.services[localIntent-4] : nullptr;
+    auto &query=s.fields;
+    auto &uim=s.uim;
+    const bool pendingUimDone=uim.end && !uim.done;
+    const bool pendingDone=(query.end && !query.done) || pendingUimDone;
+    const auto primaryBytes=query.pdState ? ThorPdrState::PacketBytes : ThorSsctlFields::PacketBytes;
+    const bool matchingServer=server && (query.pdState ?
+        server->peerServer(s.localNode,one.word(8)) && server->word(36)==ThorPdrState::Service &&
+            server->word(40)==ThorPdrState::Instance :
+        ThorSsctlFields::endpoint(*server,s.localNode,one.word(8)));
+    const bool canQuery=query.enabled && !query.end && server && !receiver.size &&
+                        s.replyDone==DoneReuse && s.peerCapacity>=primaryBytes && matchingServer;
+    const bool canUim=uim.enabled && uim.announced && !uim.end && !receiver.size &&
+                      ThorUimStatus::rootUp(query) && query.done==DoneReuse &&
+                      s.peerCapacity>=ThorUimStatus::RequestBytes;
+    const unsigned requestBytes=canUim ? ThorUimStatus::RequestBytes : primaryBytes;
+    const bool listen=one.selected && !one.stop && (!receiver.completed || replyWindow || pendingDone) &&
+                      !s.closeEnd && !s.remoteClose;
+    using Transfer=ThorPdLocator::Transfer;
+    auto &pd=s.locator;
+    Transfer pdTx=Transfer::None,pdDone=Transfer::None;
+    unsigned pdSlot=MaxIntents,deleteSlot=MaxIntents;
+    if(pd.enabled && !s.closeEnd && !s.remoteClose && !receiver.grantPending &&
+       ThorUimStatus::rootUp(query) && query.done==DoneReuse) {
+        if(!pd.published && listen && !receiver.size && !canUim) {
+            pdSlot=locatorCredit(s,ThorPdLocator::FullListBytes);
+            deleteSlot=locatorCredit(s,52,pdSlot);
+            if(pdSlot!=MaxIntents && deleteSlot!=MaxIntents) pdTx=Transfer::Publish;
+        } else if(pd.pending && pd.flight==Transfer::None && !pd.deleteEnd) {
+            pdSlot=locatorCredit(s,pd.reply.size,pd.deleteSlot);
+            if(pdSlot!=MaxIntents) pdTx=Transfer::Respond;
+            else {pdTx=Transfer::Withdraw;pdSlot=pd.deleteSlot;s.one.stop=true;}
+        } else if(pd.published && !pd.deleteEnd && (!listen || pd.responses>=LocatorSlots)) {
+            pdTx=Transfer::Withdraw;pdSlot=pd.deleteSlot;
+        }
+    }
+    const unsigned pdBytes=pdTx==Transfer::Respond ? pd.reply.size : 52;
+    bool sendPd=false,sendQuery=false,finishQuery=false;
+    // A peer can pipeline its next service allocation behind the SSCTL record.
+    // Retain that request in the FIFO and service it on the next step.
+    bool pendingRequest=false;
+    if (listen && (canQuery || canUim) && r.cursor[2]!=r.cursor[3]) {
+        packet=peek(p,r,s);
+        pendingRequest=packet.length==8 && packet.cmd()==IntentReq && packet.cid()==s.remoteId &&
+                       packet.param>0 && packet.param<=(canUim ? ThorQrtrProbe::Capacity : ThorSsctlFields::ResponseCapacity);
+        if (pendingRequest && tail<s.txHead) return Result::Waiting;
+    }
+    // Publications, responses and withdrawal have their own real remote intent.
+    // A queued control packet takes precedence except while closing or when it
+    // requests another local buffer behind a response already ready to send.
+    bool pdCanWrite=pdTx!=Transfer::None && tail==s.txHead;
+    if(pdCanWrite && r.cursor[2]!=r.cursor[3]) {
+        packet=peek(p,r,s);
+        pdCanWrite=packet.length==8 && packet.cmd()==IntentReq && packet.cid()==s.remoteId;
+        if(pdCanWrite) pendingRequest=true;
+    }
+    if(pdCanWrite) {
+        sendPd=true;tx=Data;cid=LocalId;
+    } else if (receiver.grantPending) {
+        tx=IntentReqAck; cid=LocalId;
+    } else if (!s.closeEnd && s.openEnd && ((s.established && !listen && (!pd.published || (pd.deleteEnd && (pd.deleteDone || pd.forceClose)))) || s.remoteClose)) {
+        tx=Close; cid=LocalId;
+    } else if (listen && replyWindow && !s.replyEnd && r.cursor[2]==r.cursor[3]) {
+        // Use one of the peer's advertised intents only after it read our RX_DONE.
+        if (tail!=s.txHead) return Result::Waiting;
+        tx=Data; cid=LocalId;
+    } else if (listen && (canQuery || canUim) && (r.cursor[2]==r.cursor[3] || pendingRequest) && tail==s.txHead) {
+        sendQuery=true;tx=Data;cid=LocalId;
+    } else if (r.cursor[2]!=r.cursor[3]) {
+        packet=peek(p,r,s);
+        if (!packet.length) return Result::Waiting;
+        const uint16_t id=packet.cid();
+        switch (packet.cmd()) {
+        case Open:
+            if (!packet.validName()) { blockedOpen=true;break; }
+            for (unsigned i=0;i<s.heldCount;i++) {
+                if (s.deferred[i].cid==id) return Result::Invalid;
+            }
+            if (!packet.isRouter()) {
+                if (s.ackEnd && s.remoteId==id) return Result::Invalid;
+                if (s.heldCount==MaxDeferred) { blockedOpen=true;break; }
+                // Keep the peer's request pending without binding or acknowledging
+                // its service. This edge is exclusively owned until PAS teardown.
+                defer=true;
+                if (!s.openEnd && !s.remoteClose) { tx=Open;cid=LocalId; }
+                break;
+            }
+            if (s.ackEnd || s.closeEnd) return Result::Invalid;
+            tx=OpenAck; cid=id; break;
+        // OPEN_ACK, CLOSE and CLOSE_ACK identify a channel by param1.
+        // Their second word has no receive-side meaning in this transport.
+        case Intent:
+            // Our CLOSE is on the wire. Retire the peer's credits solely to
+            // reach the closing controls. No data is sent or requested.
+            blockedIntent=!packet.validIntents(s);
+            break;
+        case Done: case DoneReuse:
+            if(id==s.remoteId && pd.deleteEnd && !pd.deleteDone && packet.param==s.retiredIds[pd.deleteSlot]) {
+                if(tail<pd.deleteEnd) return Result::Waiting;
+                pdDone=Transfer::Withdraw;break;
+            }
+            if(id==s.remoteId && pd.flight!=Transfer::None && packet.param==s.retiredIds[pd.slot]) {
+                if(tail<pd.end) return Result::Waiting;
+                pdDone=pd.flight;break;
+            }
+            finishQuery=pendingDone && s.replyDone==DoneReuse;
+            if (!s.replyEnd || (s.replyDone && !finishQuery) || id!=s.remoteId || packet.param!=s.peerIntent || s.remoteClose) {
+                s.blockedCmd=uint16_t(packet.cmd()); return Result::Blocked;
+            }
+            if (tail<(pendingUimDone ? uim.end : finishQuery ? query.end : s.replyEnd)) return Result::Waiting;
+            break;
+        case Data: case DataCont:
+            if (!one.selected || !receiver.grantEnd || receiver.completed || s.remoteClose || id!=s.remoteId ||
+                packet.param!=localIntent || !receiver.fits(packet.cmd(),packet.body[0],packet.body[1])) {
+                s.blockedCmd=uint16_t(packet.cmd()); return Result::Blocked;
+            }
+            if (tail<receiver.grantEnd) return Result::Waiting;
+            if (!packet.body[1]) { tx=Done; cid=LocalId; }
+            break;
+        case IntentReq:
+            if (listen && s.established && id==s.remoteId && packet.param && !receiver.size &&
+                packet.param<=receiveLimit(s)) {
+                // The previous packet was returned without reuse. Observe peer
+                // consumption of our RX_DONE before publishing another buffer.
+                if (serviceSlot && tail<s.txHead) return Result::Waiting;
+                tx=Intent; cid=LocalId; break;
+            }
+            if (listen && s.established && id==s.remoteId && packet.param) {
+                // Re-enter the close path for an oversized or additional request.
+                one.stop=true;
+                return Result::Waiting;
+            }
+            // A closing channel offers no receive buffers. Complete a pending
+            // same-channel allocation request using our own channel ID.
+            if (!s.established || !s.closeEnd || s.remoteClose || s.localCloseAck ||
+                id!=s.remoteId || !packet.param || s.refusals==MaxRefusals) {
+                blockedRequest=true;
+                break;
+            }
+            if (tail<s.closeEnd) return Result::Waiting;
+            tx=IntentReqAck; cid=LocalId; break;
+        case OpenAck:
+            if (id!=LocalId || !s.openEnd || s.localAck) return Result::Invalid;
+            if (tail<s.openEnd) return Result::Waiting;
+            break;
+        case Close:
+            if (!s.ackEnd || id!=s.remoteId || s.remoteClose) return Result::Invalid;
+            tx=CloseAck; cid=id; break;
+        case CloseAck:
+            if (id!=LocalId || !s.closeEnd || s.localCloseAck) return Result::Invalid;
+            if (tail<s.closeEnd) return Result::Waiting;
+            break;
+        default:
+            s.blockedCmd=uint16_t(packet.cmd()); return Result::Blocked;
+        }
+        consume=!blockedOpen && !blockedIntent && !blockedRequest;
+    } else if (s.remoteClose && !s.openEnd && tail==s.txHead) {
+        // The peer closed its half before we advertised a local channel.
+        return Result::EarlyClose;
+    } else if (!s.openEnd && !s.remoteClose) {
+        tx=Open; cid=LocalId;
+    } else return Result::Waiting;
+    const uint32_t txBytes=tx==Data ? (sendPd ? 16u+((pdBytes+7u)&~7u) : sendQuery ? 16u+((requestBytes+7u)&~7u) : 72u) : (tx==Open || tx==Intent) ? 16 : (tx ? 8 : 0);
+    const bool retire=consume && packet.cmd()==Intent;
+    const bool merge=retire && s.count && !s.log[s.count-1].tx && s.log[s.count-1].cmd==Intent;
+    const unsigned limit=s.postReplySelected && query.responseIntent ? MaxRecords :
+                         query.enabled ? QueryRecords : s.serviceWindow ? ServiceRecords : BaseRecords;
+    if (s.count+unsigned(consume && !merge)+unsigned(tx!=0)>limit) return Result::Invalid;
+    if (tx && (r.size[1]-(s.txHead-tail)<txBytes+16 || s.txHead+txBytes>=r.size[1]))
+        return Result::Waiting;
+    QcomMssGlinkSample check{};
+    rc=p.snapshot(check);
+    if (rc==QcomSmemUnstable) return Result::Waiting;
+    if (rc || !geometry(check,v.ring,s)) return Result::Epoch;
+    if (!ThorMssVersion::sameSample(r,check)) return Result::Waiting;
+    if ((consume || blockedOpen || blockedIntent || blockedRequest || pendingRequest) && !samePacket(packet,peek(p,check,s))) return Result::Epoch;
+    if (!p.live()) return Result::Epoch;
+    if (!p.inTime()) return Result::Timeout;
+    if (blockedRequest) {
+        s.blockedCmd=IntentReq;
+        s.sawBlockedRequest=true;
+        s.blockedRequestCid=packet.cid();
+        s.blockedRequestSize=packet.param;
+        s.blockedRequestAvail=r.cursor[3]-r.cursor[2];
+        return Result::Blocked;
+    }
+    if (blockedIntent) {
+        s.blockedCmd=Intent;
+        s.sawBlockedIntent=true;
+        s.blockedIntentCid=packet.cid();
+        s.blockedIntentCount=packet.param;
+        s.blockedIntentAvail=r.cursor[3]-r.cursor[2];
+        return Result::Blocked;
+    }
+    if (blockedOpen) {
+        s.blockedCmd=Open;
+        s.sawBlockedOpen=true;
+        s.blockedId=packet.cid();
+        s.blockedNameLength=uint16_t(packet.nameLength());
+        s.blockedPriority=uint16_t(packet.param>>16);
+        s.blockedAvailable=r.cursor[3]-r.cursor[2];
+        return Result::Blocked;
+    }
+    if (consume) {
+        if (defer) {
+            auto &held=s.deferred[s.heldCount++];
+            held.cid=packet.cid();
+            held.priority=uint16_t(packet.param>>16);
+            held.length=packet.nameLength();
+            for (unsigned i=0;i<held.length;i++) held.name[i]=char(packet.octet(i));
+        }
+        p.beforeConsume();
+        s.rxTail+=packet.length;
+        p.write(r.desc_offset+8,s.rxTail);
+        if (retire) {
+            for (unsigned i=0;i<packet.param;i++) {
+                const uint32_t capacity=packet.body[2*i], intent=packet.body[2*i+1];
+                if(pd.enabled) pd.capacity[s.retiredCount]=capacity;
+                s.retiredIds[s.retiredCount++]=intent;
+                if (s.localNode!=ThorQrtrProbe::Broadcast && !s.replyEnd && capacity>=ThorQrtrProbe::HelloBytes &&
+                    (!s.peerCapacity || capacity<s.peerCapacity)) {
+                    s.peerCapacity=capacity; s.peerIntent=intent; s.creditFrame=s.count+unsigned(!merge);
+                }
+            }
+            if (!merge) s.log[s.count++]={false,Intent,packet.cid(),s.txHead,s.rxTail};
+            auto &event=s.log[s.count-1];
+            event.rxTail=s.rxTail;
+            event.intentPackets++;
+            event.intentCount+=packet.param;
+        } else {
+            s.log[s.count++]={false,uint16_t(packet.cmd()),packet.cid(),s.txHead,s.rxTail,defer?s.heldCount:0};
+            auto &event=s.log[s.count-1];
+            if (packet.cmd()==IntentReq || packet.cmd()==Done || packet.cmd()==DoneReuse) event.value=packet.param;
+            event.qmi=finishQuery;event.locator=pdDone;
+            event.followup=next && ((packet.cmd()==IntentReq && tx==Intent) ||
+                                    packet.cmd()==Data || packet.cmd()==DataCont);
+            if (event.followup && serviceSlot) {
+                event.serviceIntent=uint8_t(localIntent);
+                if (packet.cmd()==IntentReq) s.grantTail[localIntent-ThorQrtrProbe::FollowupIntent-1]=tail;
+            }
+            if (packet.cmd()==Data || packet.cmd()==DataCont) {
+                event.value=packet.param;
+                event.intentCount=packet.body[0];
+                event.intentPackets=packet.body[1];
+                for (unsigned i=0;i<event.intentCount;i++) receiver.bytes[receiver.used+i]=packet.octet(8+i);
+                receiver.used+=event.intentCount;
+                receiver.remaining=event.intentPackets;
+                ++receiver.fragments;
+                receiver.completed=!receiver.remaining;
+                if (receiver.completed) {
+                    if (serviceSlot) {
+                        ThorSsctlFields::match(query,receiver,localIntent,s.localNode);
+                        ThorUimStatus::match(uim,receiver,localIntent,s.localNode);
+                        if(pd.published && !pd.deleteEnd && __builtin_popcount(pd.requestMask)<LocatorSlots) {
+                            ThorPdLocator::Wire decoded{};
+                            if(ThorPdLocator::respond(receiver,s.localNode,one.word(8),decoded)) {
+                                pd.requestMask |= 1u<<localIntent;
+                                if(!pd.pending) {pd.pending=localIntent;pd.reply=decoded;}
+                            }
+                        }
+                    }
+                    if (uim.enabled && !uim.announced && ThorUimStatus::endpoint(receiver,s.localNode,one.word(8))) {
+                        uim.announced=localIntent;
+                        uim.peerNode=receiver.word(44);
+                        uim.peerPort=receiver.word(48);
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        if (!defer) switch (packet.cmd()) {
+        case Done: case DoneReuse:
+            if(pdDone==Transfer::Withdraw) pd.deleteDone=packet.cmd();
+            else if(pdDone!=Transfer::None) {
+                if(packet.cmd()==Done) pd.capacity[pd.slot]=0;
+                pd.acknowledged=packet.cmd();pd.flight=Transfer::None;
+            } else if (pendingUimDone) uim.done=packet.cmd();
+            else if (finishQuery) query.done=packet.cmd();
+            else s.replyDone=packet.cmd();
+            break;
+        case Open:s.remoteId=packet.cid();break;
+        case OpenAck:s.localAck=true;break;
+        case Close:s.remoteClose=true;break;
+        case CloseAck:s.localCloseAck=true;break;
+        }
+    }
+    if (tx) {
+        const auto at=r.tx_offset+s.txHead;
+        p.write(at,(uint32_t(cid)<<16)|tx);
+        uint32_t param=0;
+        if (tx==Open) param=7;
+        if (tx==Intent || (tx==IntentReqAck && receiver.grantPending)) param=1;
+        if (tx==Done) param=localIntent;
+        if (tx==Data) param=sendPd ? s.retiredIds[pdSlot] : s.peerIntent;
+        p.write(at+4,param);
+        if (tx==Intent) {
+            p.write(at+8,packet.param);
+            p.write(at+12,localIntent);
+        }
+        if(sendPd) {
+            if(pdTx==Transfer::Respond) pd.reply.write(p,at);
+            else {
+                ThorPdLocator::Wire control{};
+                control.announce(s.localNode,one.word(8),pdTx==Transfer::Publish);
+                control.write(p,at);
+            }
+        } else if (sendQuery) {
+            if (canUim) ThorUimStatus::request(p,at,s.localNode,uim);
+            else if (query.pdState)
+                ThorPdrState::writeRequest(p,at,s.localNode,server->word(44),server->word(48));
+            else ThorSsctlFields::writeRequest(p,at,s.localNode,server->word(44),server->word(48));
+        } else if (tx==Data) {
+            // GLINK chunk/remaining, QRTR v1 header, HELLO command, zeroed union and alignment.
+            const uint32_t body[]={ThorQrtrProbe::HelloBytes,0,
+                1,2,s.localNode,ThorQrtrProbe::ControlPort,0,20,one.word(8),one.word(12),2,0,0,0,0,0};
+            static_assert(sizeof(body)+8==72,"GLINK QRTR frame size");
+            for (unsigned i=0;i<sizeof(body)/sizeof(body[0]);++i) p.write(at+8+i*4,body[i]);
+        }
+        if (tx==Open) {
+            // NUL-terminated "IPCRTR", with one zero alignment byte.
+            p.write(at+8,0x52435049);p.write(at+12,0x5254);
+        }
+        p.beforePublish();
+        s.txHead+=txBytes;
+        p.write(r.desc_offset+4,s.txHead);
+        s.log[s.count++]={true,tx,cid,s.txHead,s.rxTail};
+        auto &event=s.log[s.count-1];
+        event.followup=next && (tx==Done || tx==Intent || (tx==IntentReqAck && receiver.grantPending));
+        if (event.followup && serviceSlot) event.serviceIntent=uint8_t(localIntent);
+        if (tx==Intent) {
+            receiver.size=packet.param;
+            receiver.grantPending=true;
+            event.value=packet.param;
+        }
+        if (tx==Done) event.value=param;
+        if (tx==Data) {
+            event.value=param;
+            if(sendPd) {
+                event.locator=pdTx;event.intentCount=pdBytes;
+                if(pdTx==Transfer::Withdraw) pd.deleteEnd=s.txHead;
+                else {
+                    pd.flight=pdTx;pd.slot=pdSlot;pd.end=s.txHead;
+                    if(pdTx==Transfer::Publish) {pd.published=true;pd.deleteSlot=deleteSlot;}
+                    else {
+                        pd.answeredMask |= 1u<<pd.pending;pd.pending=0;++pd.responses;
+                        const unsigned remaining=pd.requestMask & ~pd.answeredMask;
+                        if(remaining) {
+                            pd.pending=unsigned(__builtin_ctz(remaining));
+                            ThorPdLocator::respond(s.services[pd.pending-3],s.localNode,one.word(8),pd.reply);
+                        }
+                    }
+                }
+            } else if (sendQuery) {
+                event.qmi=true;event.intentCount=requestBytes;
+                if (canUim) uim.end=s.txHead;
+                else {
+                    query.sourceIntent=localIntent-1;query.peerNode=server->word(44);
+                    query.peerPort=server->word(48);query.sendTail=tail;query.end=s.txHead;
+                }
+            } else {event.intentCount=ThorQrtrProbe::HelloBytes;s.replyEnd=s.txHead;}
+        }
+        switch(tx) {
+        case Open:s.openEnd=s.txHead;break;
+        case OpenAck:s.ackEnd=s.txHead;break;
+        case Close:s.closeEnd=s.txHead;break;
+        case IntentReqAck:
+            event.value=param;
+            if (receiver.grantPending) { receiver.grantPending=false; receiver.grantEnd=s.txHead; }
+            else ++s.refusals;
+            break;
+        }
+        p.kick();
+    }
+    return Result::Waiting;
+}
+}
diff --git a/ThorMssGlinkObserve.inc b/ThorMssGlinkObserve.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..938141b58ada78431ecf69bce7320bf8a5d59283
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorMssGlinkObserve.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+// The one-shot PAS owner has a separate worker for sampling. The owner's
+// READY/STOP/SHUTDOWN path only publishes a phase and never waits for it.
+enum class GlinkPhase : unsigned { BeforeReady, Ready, StopRequested, Shutdown };
+struct GlinkObservation {
+    uint64_t ticks;
+    GlinkPhase phase;
+    int rc;
+    QcomMssGlinkSample data;
+};
+static GlinkObservation glinkCold, glinkLive[2];
+static unsigned glinkPublished;
+static unsigned glinkObservedPhase;
+static bool glinkWorkerStarted;
+
+static void pasGlinkPhase(GlinkPhase stage)
+{
+    __atomic_store_n(&glinkObservedPhase,unsigned(stage),__ATOMIC_RELEASE);
+}
+static GlinkPhase pasReadGlinkPhase()
+{
+    return static_cast<GlinkPhase>(__atomic_load_n(&glinkObservedPhase,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE));
+}
+static GlinkObservation pasGlinkTake(IOMemoryMap *map,GlinkPhase stage)
+{
+    GlinkObservation record{};
+    record.phase = stage;
+    record.ticks = mach_absolute_time();
+    const QcomSmem s{reinterpret_cast<volatile uint8_t *>(map->getVirtualAddress()),0x200000};
+    record.rc = qcom_smem_mss_glink_snapshot(&s,&record.data);
+    return record;
+}
+static void pasGlinkObserve(void *arg,wait_result_t)
+{
+    auto map = static_cast<IOMemoryMap *>(arg);
+    uint64_t deadline;
+    clock_interval_to_deadline(10,NSEC_PER_SEC,&deadline);
+    unsigned captured = 0;
+    while (captured < 2 && mach_absolute_time() < deadline) {
+        const auto stage = pasReadGlinkPhase();
+        if (stage == GlinkPhase::Shutdown) break;
+        if (stage != GlinkPhase::BeforeReady) {
+            auto record = pasGlinkTake(map,stage);
+            if (stage == pasReadGlinkPhase()) {
+                glinkLive[captured++] = record;
+                __atomic_store_n(&glinkPublished,captured,__ATOMIC_RELEASE);
+            }
+        }
+        if (captured < 2) IOSleep(5);
+    }
+    map->release();
+}
+static void pasGlinkBegin(IOMemoryMap *map)
+{
+    glinkCold = pasGlinkTake(map,GlinkPhase::BeforeReady);
+    map->retain();
+    thread_t thread;
+    glinkWorkerStarted = kernel_thread_start(pasGlinkObserve,map,&thread) == KERN_SUCCESS;
+    if (glinkWorkerStarted) thread_deallocate(thread);
+    else map->release();
+}
+static void pasGlinkLog(const GlinkObservation &o)
+{
+    const auto &x = o.data;
+    const char *phase = o.phase == GlinkPhase::Ready ? "ready" :
+                        o.phase == GlinkPhase::StopRequested ? "stop-path" : "pre-auth";
+    if (o.rc) {
+        IOLog("THOR MSS GLINK OBS: phase=%s ticks=%llu rc=%d\n",phase,o.ticks,o.rc);
+        return;
+    }
+    IOLog("THOR MSS GLINK OBS: phase=%s ticks=%llu rc=0 present=%#x sizes=%u/%u/%u "
+          "part_off=%#x part_size=%u desc_off=%#x rx_off=%#x tx_tail=%u tx_head=%u rx_tail=%u rx_head=%u "
+          "version_seen=%u version=%u features=%#x "
+          "ipcrtr_open_request=%u remote_cid=%u\n",phase,o.ticks,x.present,
+          x.size[0],x.size[1],x.size[2],x.part_offset,x.part_size,x.desc_offset,x.rx_offset,x.cursor[0],x.cursor[1],x.cursor[2],x.cursor[3],
+          x.version_seen,x.version,x.features,x.ipcrtr_open_request,x.remote_cid);
+}
+static void pasGlinkReport()
+{
+    pasGlinkPhase(GlinkPhase::Shutdown);
+    const unsigned count = __atomic_load_n(&glinkPublished,__ATOMIC_ACQUIRE);
+    pasGlinkLog(glinkCold);
+    for (unsigned i=0; i<count; ++i) pasGlinkLog(glinkLive[i]);
+    IOLog("THOR MSS GLINK OBS: worker=%u live_samples=%u\n",unsigned(glinkWorkerStarted),count);
+}
diff --git a/ThorMssServe.inc b/ThorMssServe.inc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..580f6a72a44d832f6da04e4ee786bc10ed3610d0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ThorMssServe.inc
@@ -0,0 +1,653 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
+// v228: the two AP-side services the modem waits for before it finishes booting.
+//
+// Up to v227 the modem was brought to READY, its QRTR HELLO was answered by a
+// bounded recorder, two of its services (SSCTL 43, SERVREG 66) were logged and it
+// was stopped again. The same two services are all MIX Fold 2 (same SoC family,
+// same MPSS generation) sees until an AP-side rmtfs serves the modem's EFS; with
+// one, its modem advertises 45 services and stays up in OFFLINE mode.
+//
+// This runs on the QcomGlink transport that is byte-identical in Pong, Fold 2 and
+// Thor. Protocol handling follows Fold 2's verified ZizhanMpss.cpp/ZizhanRmtfs.h:
+//   * QRTR HELLO is answered and the AP announces a SERVREG locator (service 0x40,
+//     instance 0x101, from Thor's own modem_a directory) and rmtfs (service 14,
+//     instance 1).
+//   * rmtfs answers OPEN/CLOSE/RW_IOVEC/ALLOC_BUFF/GET_DEV_ERROR. Each EFS
+//     partition (modemst1, modemst2, fsg, fsc) is read once into a RAM shadow;
+//     modem writes land in the shadow only, so nothing on the phone's storage
+//     changes. The shared buffer is Thor's reserved RMTFS lease, lent to the modem
+//     with the secure-world MP_ASSIGN call first.
+//   * After 20 s two read-only QMI requests are sent when the modem advertises
+//     the services: DMS Get Operating Mode (0x2d) and UIM Get Card Status (0x2f).
+// Nothing here sends a state-changing QMI message, so no radio transmit.
+//
+// The worker returns to the unchanged stop path (SMP2P stop, PAS shutdown, AOSS
+// load off). Every exit leaves the partitions and the phone's storage untouched.
+#include "QcomGlink.h"
+#include "ThorPdLocator.h"
+#include "ThorUimStatus.h"
+
+namespace ThorServe {
+constexpr uint32_t kControl = 0xfffffffeu, kApps = 1, kModem = 0;
+// v237: the modem's SMEM host id is 1 (every other partition lookup in QcomSmem.c uses it);
+// kModem is its QRTR node id (0).  The APPS-to-modem partition was looked up with 0 and never found.
+constexpr uint32_t kSmemModemHost = 1;
+constexpr uint32_t kPdmPort = 0x4002, kRmtfsPort = 0x4001, kDmsPort = 0x4003, kUimPort = 0x4004;
+constexpr uint32_t kIntentBytes = 0x4400, kIntents = 4, kSector = 512, kFifoBytes = 0x4000;
+constexpr unsigned kMaxReply = 384, kMaxChunk = 128 * 1024, kMaxPart = 16 * 1024 * 1024;
+constexpr uint32_t kVmidHlos = 3, kVmidMssMsa = 15, kPermRw = 0x6;
+// v237: the audio processor and the battery service start after this trial, so it is held to 24 s
+// (was 60 s; the read-only queries go out at 12 s instead of 20 s).
+constexpr unsigned kWatchMs = 24000, kEarlyMs = 25000, kQueryMs = 12000;
+constexpr unsigned kDmsService = 2, kNasService = 3, kWdsService = 1, kUimService = 11;
+// BSD errno values; this translation unit does not include <sys/errno.h>.
+constexpr int kErrIo = 5, kErrTooBig = 7, kErrNoMemory = 12, kErrNotSupported = 45;
+
+QcomGlink gGlink;
+QcomGlinkChannel *gIpcrtr;
+uint8_t gStore[kIntents * kIntentBytes];
+volatile uint8_t *gSmem;
+volatile uint32_t *gDoorbell;
+IOMemoryMap *gBufMap, *gArgsMap;
+volatile uint8_t *gBuf, *gArgs;
+uint64_t gBufPhys, gBufBytes;
+bool gOn, gHello, gHelloQueued, gAnnounced, gAssigned, gRfsReady, gDmsAsked;
+uint32_t gDmsPeer, gUimPeer, gServiceMask, gDmsAnswered, gUimAnswered;
+struct Part { const char *path; uint8_t *shadow; uint64_t bytes, allocated; bool open; };
+Part gParts[4] = {{"/boot/modem_fs1", nullptr, 0, 0, false}, {"/boot/modem_fs2", nullptr, 0, 0, false},
+                  {"/boot/modem_fsg", nullptr, 0, 0, false}, {"/boot/modem_fsc", nullptr, 0, 0, false}};
+QcomSmemPartition gPart{};
+// Packets the remote could not take yet (no free intent, no FIFO room), oldest first.
+struct Pending { bool valid; uint32_t type, node, port, from; uint16_t bytes; uint8_t data[kMaxReply]; } gPending[4];
+unsigned gCtlLogged, gDataLogged, gServers, gPdmRequests, gReqs, gReads, gWrites, gRefused, gDropped, gCorrupt;
+unsigned gWordReads, gWordSkipped;   // v237: modem entry samples read, and skipped as unstable or unpublished
+uint64_t gReadBytes, gWriteBytes, gMaxIoBytes;
+int gSmemPart;
+
+static uint64_t elapsedMs(uint64_t since)
+{
+    uint64_t ns = 0;
+    absolutetime_to_nanoseconds(mach_absolute_time() - since, &ns);
+    return ns / 1000000;
+}
+static void kick(void *)
+{
+    __asm__ volatile("dsb oshst" ::: "memory");
+    *gDoorbell = qcom_ipcc_id(2, QCOM_IPCC_SIGNAL_GLINK_QMP);
+    __asm__ volatile("dsb oshst" ::: "memory");
+}
+static uint32_t get32(const uint8_t *p) { uint32_t v; memcpy(&v, p, 4); return v; }
+static uint16_t get16(const uint8_t *p) { return uint16_t(p[0] | (p[1] << 8)); }
+static void put16(uint8_t *p, uint32_t n) { p[0] = uint8_t(n); p[1] = uint8_t(n >> 8); }
+
+/* One QRTR packet: header (version, type, source, confirm, length, destination), then a 4-byte aligned body. */
+static bool sendNow(uint32_t type, uint32_t dstNode, uint32_t dstPort, uint32_t srcPort, const uint8_t *payload, uint32_t len)
+{
+    static uint8_t pkt[32 + kMaxReply];
+    if (len > kMaxReply) return false;
+    const uint32_t h[8] = {1, type, kApps, srcPort, 0, len, dstNode, dstPort};
+    memcpy(pkt, h, 32);
+    memcpy(pkt + 32, payload, len);
+    const uint32_t total = (32 + len + 3) & ~3u;
+    for (uint32_t i = 32 + len; i < total; ++i) pkt[i] = 0;
+    return qcom_glink_send(&gGlink, gIpcrtr, pkt, total) == QcomGlinkOk;
+}
+/* A packet that cannot go out yet is kept, in order, and retried after every poll. */
+static bool send(uint32_t type, uint32_t node, uint32_t port, uint32_t from, const uint8_t *payload, uint32_t len)
+{
+    if (gIpcrtr && gIpcrtr->up && sendNow(type, node, port, from, payload, len)) return true;
+    unsigned slot = 4;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) if (!gPending[i].valid) { slot = i; break; }
+    if (slot == 4 || len > kMaxReply) { ++gDropped; return false; }
+    gPending[slot] = {};
+    gPending[slot].valid = true; gPending[slot].type = type; gPending[slot].node = node;
+    gPending[slot].port = port; gPending[slot].from = from; gPending[slot].bytes = uint16_t(len);
+    memcpy(gPending[slot].data, payload, len);
+    return false;
+}
+static unsigned pending()
+{
+    unsigned n = 0;
+    for (const auto &p : gPending) n += p.valid;
+    return n;
+}
+static void flush()
+{
+    unsigned i = 0;
+    while (i < 4 && gPending[i].valid) {
+        if (!(gIpcrtr && gIpcrtr->up)) return;
+        Pending &p = gPending[i];
+        if (sendNow(p.type, p.node, p.port, p.from, p.data, p.bytes)) {
+            if (p.type == 2) gHello = true;   // our HELLO finally left
+            for (unsigned j = i; j < 3; ++j) gPending[j] = gPending[j + 1];
+            gPending[3] = {};
+            // Stay here: the next waiting packet has moved into this slot.
+        } else ++i;
+    }
+}
+static void sendHello()
+{
+    uint32_t pkt[13] = {};
+    pkt[0] = 1; pkt[1] = 2;                 // version 1, HELLO
+    pkt[2] = kApps; pkt[3] = kControl;      // from APPS' control port
+    pkt[5] = 20;                            // 16-byte node mask after the command
+    pkt[6] = 0xffffffffu; pkt[7] = kControl;
+    pkt[8] = 2;                             // QRTR_TYPE_HELLO
+    // The QRTR header is built by sendNow(); the HELLO body is the command and its node mask.
+    gHello = send(2, 0xffffffffu, kControl, kControl, reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(pkt + 8), sizeof pkt - 8 * sizeof pkt[0]);
+    gHelloQueued = true;
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: qrtr hello sent=%u\n", unsigned(gHello));
+}
+static void announce()
+{
+    const uint32_t pdm[5] = {4, ThorPdLocator::Service, ThorPdLocator::Instance, kApps, kPdmPort};
+    const uint32_t rfs[5] = {4, 14, 0x1, kApps, kRmtfsPort};
+    const bool a = send(4, kModem, kControl, kControl, reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(pdm), sizeof pdm);
+    const bool b = gRfsReady && send(4, kModem, kControl, kControl, reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(rfs), sizeof rfs);
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: announced locator=%u service=%#x instance=%#x port=%#x rmtfs=%u service=14 instance=1 port=%#x "
+          "buffer=%#llx+%#llx assigned=%u\n", unsigned(a), ThorPdLocator::Service, ThorPdLocator::Instance, kPdmPort,
+          unsigned(b), kRmtfsPort, (unsigned long long)gBufPhys, (unsigned long long)gBufBytes, unsigned(gAssigned));
+}
+
+/* SERVREG locator: which protection domains provide a service. Thor's table is its own modem_a registry. */
+static void pdmHandle(uint32_t srcNode, uint32_t srcPort, const uint8_t *q, uint32_t n)
+{
+    if (n < 7 || q[0] != 0) return;
+    const uint16_t txn = get16(q + 1), msg = get16(q + 3), len = get16(q + 5);
+    if (7u + len > n) return;
+    const uint8_t *named = nullptr;
+    unsigned length = 0;
+    uint32_t offset = 0;
+    bool offsetSeen = false;
+    for (uint32_t at = 7; at + 3 <= 7u + len;) {
+        const uint8_t t = q[at];
+        const uint16_t l = get16(q + at + 1);
+        at += 3;
+        if (l > 7u + len - at) break;
+        if (t == 0x01 && !named && l && l <= 64) { named = q + at; length = l; }
+        else if (t == 0x10 && !offsetSeen && l == 4) { offsetSeen = true; offset = get32(q + at); }
+        at += l;
+    }
+    ++gPdmRequests;
+    static uint8_t r[32 + kMaxReply];
+    uint32_t o = 7;
+    auto tlv = [&](uint8_t t, const void *v, uint16_t l) {
+        if (o + 3u + l > sizeof r) return;   // v237: the reply never leaves its buffer
+        r[o] = t; put16(r + o + 1, l); memcpy(r + o + 3, v, l); o += 3 + l;
+    };
+    const uint16_t failure = msg == 0x21 ? 0u : 94u;   // QMI_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED_V01
+    const uint8_t answer[4] = {uint8_t(failure != 0), 0, uint8_t(failure), uint8_t(failure >> 8)};
+    tlv(0x02, answer, 4);
+    const uint8_t mask = !failure && named ? ThorPdLocator::providers(named, length) : 0;
+    unsigned total = 0, skipped = 0, listed = 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 7; ++i) if (mask & (1u << i)) ++total;
+    if (!failure) {
+        const uint16_t all = uint16_t(total), revision = 1;
+        tlv(0x10, &all, 2);
+        tlv(0x11, &revision, 2);
+        uint8_t list[ThorPdLocator::MaxWire];
+        unsigned L = 1;                      // [0] is the number of entries in this reply
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 7; ++i) {
+            if (!(mask & (1u << i)) || (skipped++ < offset)) continue;
+            const unsigned chars = unsigned(strlen(ThorPdLocator::domains[i].name));
+            if (L + chars + 10 > sizeof list) break;
+            list[L++] = uint8_t(chars);
+            memcpy(list + L, ThorPdLocator::domains[i].name, chars);
+            L += chars;
+            const uint32_t instance = ThorPdLocator::domains[i].instance, data = 0;
+            memcpy(list + L, &instance, 4); L += 4;
+            list[L++] = 0;                    // service_data_valid
+            memcpy(list + L, &data, 4); L += 4;
+            ++listed;
+        }
+        list[0] = uint8_t(listed);            // a paged reply carries fewer entries than the total
+        tlv(0x12, list, uint16_t(L));
+    }
+    r[0] = 2; put16(r + 1, txn); put16(r + 3, msg); put16(r + 5, o - 7);
+    (void)send(1, srcNode, srcPort, kPdmPort, r, o);
+    char name[65] = {};
+    if (named) { memcpy(name, named, length); name[length] = 0; }
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: locator request msg=%#x txn=%u name='%s' offset=%u from=%u:%#x -> total=%u listed=%u\n",
+          msg, txn, name, offset, srcNode, srcPort, total, listed);
+}
+
+/* ---- rmtfs ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+static int openPart(Part &p, unsigned slot)
+{
+    if (p.open) return 0;
+    if (!pong_ufs_factory_nv) return kErrNotSupported;
+    uint64_t bytes = 0;
+    int rc = pong_ufs_factory_nv(slot, 0, nullptr, 0, &bytes);
+    if (rc) return rc;
+    if (!bytes || bytes > kMaxPart) return kErrTooBig;
+    p.shadow = static_cast<uint8_t *>(IOMallocData(bytes));
+    if (!p.shadow) return kErrNoMemory;
+    p.allocated = bytes;
+    for (uint64_t off = 0; off < bytes && !rc; off += kMaxChunk) {
+        const uint32_t count = uint32_t(bytes - off < kMaxChunk ? bytes - off : kMaxChunk);
+        uint64_t whole = 0;
+        rc = pong_ufs_factory_nv(slot, off, p.shadow + off, count, &whole);
+        if (!rc && whole != bytes) rc = kErrIo;
+    }
+    if (rc) { IOFreeData(p.shadow, p.allocated); p.shadow = nullptr; p.allocated = 0; return rc; }
+    p.bytes = bytes;
+    p.open = true;
+    return 0;
+}
+static void closeParts()
+{
+    for (auto &p : gParts) {
+        if (p.shadow) IOFreeData(p.shadow, p.allocated);
+        p.shadow = nullptr; p.bytes = p.allocated = 0; p.open = false;
+    }
+}
+/* One QMI request to our rmtfs port. Builds the response and sends it. */
+static void rfsHandle(uint32_t srcNode, uint32_t srcPort, const uint8_t *q, uint32_t n)
+{
+    if (n < 7 || q[0] != 0) return;
+    const uint16_t txn = get16(q + 1), msg = get16(q + 3), len = get16(q + 5);
+    if (7u + len > n) return;
+    const uint8_t *tl[8] = {};
+    uint16_t tlen[8] = {};
+    for (uint32_t at = 7; at + 3 <= 7u + len;) {
+        const uint8_t t = q[at];
+        const uint16_t l = get16(q + at + 1);
+        if (at + 3 + l > 7u + len) break;
+        if (t < 8) { tl[t] = q + at + 3; tlen[t] = l; }
+        at += 3 + l;
+    }
+    ++gReqs;
+    static uint8_t r[32 + kMaxReply];
+    uint32_t o = 7;
+    uint16_t result = 0, error = 0;
+    uint8_t extraT = 0, extra[8] = {}, extraL = 0;
+    switch (msg) {
+    case 0x0001: {   // OPEN: path -> caller id
+        char path[48] = "";
+        if (tl[1]) {
+            const uint32_t k = tlen[1] < sizeof path - 1 ? tlen[1] : sizeof path - 1;
+            memcpy(path, tl[1], k); path[k] = 0;
+        }
+        int which = -1;
+        for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) if (!strcmp(path, gParts[i].path)) which = i;
+        const int rc = which >= 0 ? openPart(gParts[which], unsigned(which)) : -1;
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs open '%s' -> id=%d rc=%d bytes=%llu shadow=%u\n", path, which, rc,
+              which >= 0 ? (unsigned long long)gParts[which].bytes : 0ull, which >= 0 && gParts[which].open);
+        if (rc) { result = 1; error = 0x10; ++gRefused; }
+        else { extraT = 0x10; const uint32_t id = uint32_t(which); memcpy(extra, &id, 4); extraL = 4; }
+        break;
+    }
+    case 0x0002:     // CLOSE
+        break;
+    case 0x0003: {   // RW_IOVEC: caller id, direction (0 read, 1 write), iovec[] {sector, buffer offset, sectors}
+        const uint32_t id = tl[1] && tlen[1] >= 4 ? get32(tl[1]) : 99;
+        const uint8_t dir = tl[2] && tlen[2] >= 1 ? tl[2][0] : 0xff;
+        bool ok = id < 4 && gParts[id].open && gRfsReady && tl[3] && tlen[3] >= 1 && dir <= 1;
+        const uint8_t count = ok ? tl[3][0] : 0;
+        ok = ok && 1u + 12u * count <= tlen[3];
+        uint64_t moved = 0;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; ok && i < count; ++i) {
+            const uint8_t *v = tl[3] + 1 + 12 * i;
+            // phys_offset is the absolute physical address inside the buffer ALLOC_BUFF handed out.
+            const uint64_t sector = get32(v), phys = get32(v + 4), bytes = uint64_t(get32(v + 8)) * kSector;
+            if (!bytes || phys < gBufPhys || phys - gBufPhys + bytes > gBufBytes ||
+                sector * kSector + bytes > gParts[id].bytes || ((phys - gBufPhys) & 7)) {
+                IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs iovec out of range id=%u dir=%u sector=%llu phys=%#llx bytes=%llu\n",
+                      id, dir, (unsigned long long)sector, (unsigned long long)phys, (unsigned long long)bytes);
+                ok = false; break;
+            }
+            const uint64_t off = phys - gBufPhys;
+            uint8_t *shadow = gParts[id].shadow + sector * kSector;
+            if (dir == 0) {
+                // EFS partition into the modem's buffer.
+                for (uint64_t b = 0; b < bytes; b += 8) {
+                    uint64_t w; memcpy(&w, shadow + b, 8);
+                    *reinterpret_cast<volatile uint64_t *>(gBuf + off + b) = w;
+                }
+                gReadBytes += bytes; ++gReads;
+            } else {
+                // The modem's write lands in the RAM shadow only.
+                for (uint64_t b = 0; b < bytes; b += 8) {
+                    const uint64_t w = *reinterpret_cast<const volatile uint64_t *>(gBuf + off + b);
+                    memcpy(shadow + b, &w, 8);
+                }
+                gWriteBytes += bytes; ++gWrites;
+            }
+            moved += bytes;
+        }
+        if (moved > gMaxIoBytes) gMaxIoBytes = moved;
+        if (!ok) { result = 1; error = 0x10; ++gRefused;
+                  IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs rw_iovec refused id=%u dir=%u count=%u\n", id, dir, count); }
+        break;
+    }
+    case 0x0004: {   // ALLOC_BUFF: caller id, size -> physical address
+        const uint32_t size = tl[2] && tlen[2] >= 4 ? get32(tl[2]) : 0;
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs alloc_buff size=%u -> %#llx (assigned=%u)\n", size,
+              (unsigned long long)gBufPhys, unsigned(gAssigned));
+        if (!size || size > gBufBytes || !gRfsReady) { result = 1; error = 0x10; ++gRefused; }
+        else { extraT = 0x10; const uint64_t a = gBufPhys; memcpy(extra, &a, 8); extraL = 8; }
+        break;
+    }
+    case 0x0005:     // GET_DEV_ERROR -> status 0
+        extraT = 0x10; extra[0] = 0; extraL = 1;
+        break;
+    default:
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs unknown msg=%#x len=%u\n", msg, len);
+        result = 1; error = 0x1e;
+    }
+    r[o] = 0x02; put16(r + o + 1, 4); memcpy(r + o + 3, &result, 2); memcpy(r + o + 5, &error, 2);
+    o += 7;
+    if (extraT) { r[o] = extraT; put16(r + o + 1, extraL); memcpy(r + o + 3, extra, extraL); o += 3 + extraL; }
+    r[0] = 2; put16(r + 1, txn); put16(r + 3, msg); put16(r + 5, o - 7);
+    (void)send(1, srcNode, srcPort, kRmtfsPort, r, o);
+}
+
+/* Lend the shared buffer to the modem (HLOS RW + MSS_MSA RW), as Linux qcom_scm_assign_mem does for rmtfs. */
+static bool assignBuffer(uint64_t argsPhys)
+{
+    volatile uint8_t *a = gArgs;
+    const uint64_t mem[2] = {gBufPhys, gBufBytes};
+    const uint32_t src[1] = {kVmidHlos};
+    struct Perm { uint32_t vmid, perm; uint64_t ctx; uint32_t ctxSize, unused; } dst[2] = {
+        {kVmidHlos, kPermRw, 0, 0, 0}, {kVmidMssMsa, kPermRw, 0, 0, 0}};
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof mem; ++i) a[i] = reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(mem)[i];
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof src; ++i) a[0x100 + i] = reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(src)[i];
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof dst; ++i) a[0x200 + i] = reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(dst)[i];
+    volatile uint64_t *extra = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint64_t *>(a + 0x800);
+    extra[0] = sizeof src; extra[1] = argsPhys + 0x200; extra[2] = sizeof dst; extra[3] = 0;
+    __asm__ volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+    // QCOM_SCM_SVC_MP (0x0c) / QCOM_SCM_MP_ASSIGN (0x16): seven arguments, the fourth onwards in a
+    // memory block whose physical address goes in x5. Types: RO, VAL, RO, VAL, RO, VAL, VAL.
+    const uint32_t arginfo = 7u | (1u << 4) | (1u << 8) | (1u << 12);
+    if (!pong_scm_call_lock()) return false;
+    int64_t x0 = -1; uint64_t x1 = 0;
+    bool held = true;
+    for (unsigned busy = 0; busy < 20; ++busy) {
+        uint64_t function = qcom_scm_fn(0x0cu, 0x16u), session = 0;
+        unsigned resumes = 0;
+        for (;;) {
+            register uint64_t r0 __asm__("x0") = function, r1 __asm__("x1") = arginfo, r2 __asm__("x2") = argsPhys,
+                r3 __asm__("x3") = sizeof mem, r4 __asm__("x4") = argsPhys + 0x100, r5 __asm__("x5") = argsPhys + 0x800,
+                r6 __asm__("x6") = session, r7 __asm__("x7") = 0;
+#ifndef THOR_SERVE_HOST_TEST
+            __asm__ volatile("smc #0" : "+r"(r0), "+r"(r1), "+r"(r2), "+r"(r3), "+r"(r4), "+r"(r5), "+r"(r6), "+r"(r7)
+                             :: "x8", "x9", "x10", "x11", "x12", "x13", "x14", "x15", "x16", "x17", "memory");
+#else
+            r0 = 0; r1 = 0;   // the host harness has no secure world: the assignment is accepted
+#endif
+            x0 = int64_t(r0); x1 = r1;
+            if (x0 != QCOM_SCM_INTERRUPTED || ++resumes > 100000) break;
+            function = QCOM_SCM_INTERRUPTED;
+            session = r6;
+        }
+        if (x0 != QCOM_SCM_V2_EBUSY) break;
+        // v237: the secure-call gate is shared; a busy secure world must not hold others out
+        // while this thread waits for its retry.
+        pong_scm_call_unlock(); held = false;
+        IOSleep(30);
+        if (!pong_scm_call_lock()) break;
+        held = true;
+    }
+    if (held) pong_scm_call_unlock();
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: assign buffer=%#llx+%#llx to HLOS+MSS_MSA x0=%lld x1=%#llx\n",
+          (unsigned long long)gBufPhys, (unsigned long long)gBufBytes, (long long)x0, (unsigned long long)x1);
+    return x0 == 0;
+}
+static bool mapRange(IOMemoryMap *&map, volatile uint8_t *&va, uint64_t phys, uint64_t bytes)
+{
+    IODeviceMemory *memory = IODeviceMemory::withRange(phys, bytes);
+    if (!memory) return false;
+    map = memory->map(kIOMapAnywhere | kIOMapInhibitCache);
+    memory->release();
+    va = map ? reinterpret_cast<volatile uint8_t *>(map->getVirtualAddress()) : nullptr;
+    return va != nullptr && map->getLength() == bytes;
+}
+static bool rfsSetup()
+{
+    // The secure call's argument block takes the last page of the modem metadata
+    // lease: INIT_IMAGE consumed the 5,884-byte metadata long before this runs.
+    uint64_t metadata = 0;
+    if (!PongLowDma::rmtfsAddress(gBufPhys) || !PongLowDma::modemMetadataAddress(metadata) ||
+        PongLowDma::ModemMetadataBytes < 0x2000 ||
+        !mapRange(gArgsMap, gArgs, metadata + PongLowDma::ModemMetadataBytes - 0x1000, 0x1000)) {
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs lease unavailable metadata=%#llx\n", (unsigned long long)metadata);
+        return false;
+    }
+    gBufBytes = PongLowDma::RmtfsBytes;
+    if (!mapRange(gBufMap, gBuf, gBufPhys, gBufBytes)) {
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: rmtfs buffer map failed\n");
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (uint64_t i = 0; i < gBufBytes; i += 8) *reinterpret_cast<volatile uint64_t *>(gBuf + i) = 0;
+    gAssigned = assignBuffer(metadata + PongLowDma::ModemMetadataBytes - 0x1000);
+    gRfsReady = gAssigned;
+    return gRfsReady;
+}
+static void rfsTeardown()
+{
+    closeParts();
+    if (gBufMap) { __asm__ volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory"); gBufMap->release(); gBufMap = nullptr; }
+    if (gArgsMap) { gArgsMap->release(); gArgsMap = nullptr; }
+    gBuf = gArgs = nullptr;
+}
+
+/* ---- QRTR on IPCRTR ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
+static void state(void *, QcomGlinkChannel *, int up)
+{
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: glink IPCRTR %s rx=%u tx=%u version_agreed=%u\n", up ? "up" : "down",
+          gGlink.rx_messages, gGlink.tx_messages, unsigned(gGlink.version_agreed));
+}
+/* Read-only answers: QMI result, then the one field each request asks for. */
+static void qmiAnswer(uint32_t service, uint32_t srcNode, uint32_t srcPort, const uint8_t *q, uint32_t n)
+{
+    if (n < 7 || q[0] != 2) return;
+    const uint16_t txn = get16(q + 1), msg = get16(q + 3), len = get16(q + 5);
+    if (7u + len > n) return;
+    uint16_t result = 0xffff, error = 0xffff;
+    uint8_t mode = 0xff;
+    ThorUimStatus::Query card{};
+    bool cardsParsed = false;
+    for (uint32_t at = 7; at + 3 <= 7u + len;) {
+        const uint8_t t = q[at];
+        const uint16_t l = get16(q + at + 1);
+        at += 3;
+        if (l > 7u + len - at) break;
+        if (t == 0x02 && l == 4) { result = get16(q + at); error = get16(q + at + 2); }
+        else if (t == 0x01 && msg == 0x2d && l >= 1) mode = q[at];
+        else if (t == 0x10 && msg == 0x2f) cardsParsed = ThorUimStatus::cards(q + at, l, card);
+        at += l;
+    }
+    if (service == kDmsService) {
+        ++gDmsAnswered;
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: dms operating_mode msg=%#x txn=%u result=%u error=%u mode=%u from=%u:%#x\n",
+              msg, txn, result, error, mode, srcNode, srcPort);
+    } else {
+        ++gUimAnswered;
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: uim card_status msg=%#x txn=%u result=%u error=%u parsed=%u slots=%u present=%u absent=%u fault=%u from=%u:%#x\n",
+              msg, txn, result, error, unsigned(cardsParsed), card.slots, card.present, card.absent, card.fault, srcNode, srcPort);
+    }
+}
+static void receive(void *, QcomGlinkChannel *, const uint8_t *d, uint32_t n)
+{
+    if (n < 32) { ++gDataLogged; return; }
+    uint32_t h[8];
+    memcpy(h, d, sizeof h);
+    if (h[0] != 1) return;
+    const uint32_t type = h[1];
+    if (type == 1) {   // DATA (QMI)
+        if (h[5] > n - 32) return;
+        if (h[7] == kPdmPort) { pdmHandle(h[2], h[3], d + 32, h[5]); return; }
+        if (h[7] == kRmtfsPort) { rfsHandle(h[2], h[3], d + 32, h[5]); return; }
+        if (h[7] == kDmsPort) { qmiAnswer(kDmsService, h[2], h[3], d + 32, h[5]); return; }
+        if (h[7] == kUimPort) { qmiAnswer(kUimService, h[2], h[3], d + 32, h[5]); return; }
+        if (gDataLogged++ < 12)
+            IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: qrtr data to AP port %#x from %u:%#x size=%u\n", h[7], h[2], h[3], h[5]);
+        return;
+    }
+    uint32_t c[5] = {};
+    const uint32_t body = n - 32 < sizeof c ? n - 32 : sizeof c;
+    memcpy(c, d + 32, body);
+    if (type == 4 && body >= sizeof c) {   // NEW_SERVER from the modem
+        ++gServers;
+        const uint32_t service = c[1], port = c[4];
+        const uint32_t bit = service < 32 ? 1u << service : 0;
+        gServiceMask |= bit;
+        if (service == kDmsService) gDmsPeer = port;
+        if (service == kUimService) gUimPeer = port;
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: modem server service=%u instance=%#x node=%u port=%#x\n", service, c[2], c[3], port);
+        return;
+    }
+    if (gCtlLogged++ < 40)
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: qrtr ctrl type=%u from %u:%#x cmd=%u a=%#x b=%#x c=%#x d=%#x\n",
+              type, h[2], h[3], c[0], c[1], c[2], c[3], c[4]);
+    if (type == 2 && !gHelloQueued) sendHello();   // the services are announced once it is out
+}
+static int linkStart(IOMemoryMap *smemMap, IOMemoryMap *mutexMap, IOMemoryMap *ipccMap)
+{
+    gSmem = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint8_t *>(smemMap->getVirtualAddress());
+    gDoorbell = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(ipccMap->getVirtualAddress() + QCOM_IPCC_SEND);
+    const QcomSmem smem{gSmem, 0x200000};
+    QcomSmemPartition part{};
+    int rc = qcom_smem_partition(&smem, QCOM_SMEM_HOST_APPS, kSmemModemHost, &part);
+    gSmemPart = rc;
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V237: partition lookup apps=%u modem-host=%u rc=%d\n",
+          unsigned(QCOM_SMEM_HOST_APPS), kSmemModemHost, rc);
+    if (rc) { IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: smem partition rc=%d\n", rc); return rc; }
+    gPart = part;
+    auto *mutex = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(mutexMap->getVirtualAddress());
+    if (pong_smem_lock(mutex)) {
+        rc = qcom_smem_alloc(&smem, &part, 478, 32);
+        if (rc == QcomSmemOk || rc == QcomSmemExists) rc = qcom_smem_alloc(&smem, &part, 479, kFifoBytes);
+        pong_smem_unlock(mutex);
+    } else rc = QcomSmemUnstable;
+    uint32_t descOffset = 0, descBytes = 0, txOffset = 0, txBytes = 0;
+    int found = qcom_smem_find(&smem, &part, 478, &descOffset, &descBytes);
+    const int tx = qcom_smem_find(&smem, &part, 479, &txOffset, &txBytes);
+    if ((rc != QcomSmemOk && rc != QcomSmemExists) || found || tx || descBytes < 16 || !txBytes || (txBytes & 7)) {
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: glink smem alloc=%d desc=%d/%u tx=%d/%u\n", rc, found, descBytes, tx, txBytes);
+        return rc ? rc : (found ? found : QcomSmemMissing);
+    }
+    volatile uint32_t *desc = reinterpret_cast<volatile uint32_t *>(gSmem + descOffset);
+    const QcomGlinkFifo txFifo = {desc + 1, desc + 0, gSmem + txOffset, txBytes}, rxFifo = {desc + 3, desc + 2, nullptr, 0};
+    qcom_glink_init(&gGlink, txFifo, rxFifo, kick, nullptr);
+    static const QcomGlinkClient client = {state, receive};
+    gIpcrtr = qcom_glink_channel(&gGlink, "IPCRTR", kIntentBytes, kIntents, gStore, &client, nullptr, 1);
+    gOn = gIpcrtr != nullptr;
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: glink start desc=%#x/%u tx=%#x/%u channel=%u intents=%ux%#x\n",
+          descOffset, descBytes, txOffset, txBytes, unsigned(gOn), kIntents, kIntentBytes);
+    return gOn ? 0 : QcomSmemNoSignal;
+}
+static void logCrash(const QcomSmem &smem)
+{
+    QcomSmemPartition global{};
+    uint32_t at = 0, bytes = 0;
+    if (qcom_smem_partition(&smem, QCOM_SMEM_HOST_GLOBAL, QCOM_SMEM_HOST_GLOBAL, &global) ||
+        qcom_smem_find(&smem, &global, 421, &at, &bytes) || !bytes) {
+        IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: crash-reason none\n");
+        return;
+    }
+    char text[121];
+    size_t n = 0;
+    const uint32_t limit = bytes < sizeof text - 1 ? bytes : sizeof text - 1;
+    for (; n < limit; ++n) {
+        const char c = char(gSmem[at + n]);
+        if (!c) break;
+        text[n] = c >= 32 && c < 127 ? c : '.';
+    }
+    text[n] = 0;
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: crash-reason '%s'\n", text);
+}
+
+/* After every poll: send what the remote can take now, and announce our two services
+   once our HELLO has actually left. */
+static void pump()
+{
+    flush();
+    if (gHello && !gAnnounced) { gAnnounced = true; announce(); flush(); }
+}
+
+/* Called by the PAS worker between READY and the stop path. Returns 0 when the
+   transport ran; either way the caller continues to the unchanged stop path. */
+static int run(IOMemoryMap *smemMap, IOMemoryMap *mutexMap, IOMemoryMap *ipccMap)
+{
+    int rc = linkStart(smemMap, mutexMap, ipccMap);
+    if (rc) return rc;
+    (void)rfsSetup();
+    const QcomSmem smem{gSmem, 0x200000};
+    const uint64_t began = mach_absolute_time();
+    uint64_t nextReport = began;
+    uint32_t lastWord = 0xffffffffu;
+    unsigned settleAt = 0;
+    const uint32_t wanted = (1u << kDmsService) | (1u << kNasService) | (1u << kWdsService) | (1u << kUimService);
+    const char *reason = "watch-complete";
+    for (;;) {
+        if (!gGlink.rx.data) {
+            uint32_t rx = 0, bytes = 0;
+            if (!qcom_smem_find(&smem, &gPart, 480, &rx, &bytes) && bytes >= 8 && !(bytes & 7))
+                qcom_glink_set_rx(&gGlink, gSmem + rx, bytes);
+        }
+        if (qcom_glink_poll(&gGlink) == QcomGlinkCorrupt) { ++gCorrupt; reason = "glink-corrupt"; break; }
+        pump();
+        uint32_t stop = 0, word = 0;
+        const int host = qcom_smem_mss_host_stop(&smem, &stop);
+        const int remote = qcom_smem_mss_inbound(&smem, &word);
+        if (host || stop || remote == QcomSmemMissing) {
+            reason = remote == QcomSmemMissing ? "modem-smp2p-gone" : "stop-bit-changed"; break;
+        }
+        // v237: a sample taken while the modem allocates shared memory comes back "unstable" and one
+        // taken before the modem publishes its entry "unpublished"; neither means the modem is gone
+        // (only a missing entry does), so such a pass is skipped instead of ending the trial.
+        if (!remote) {
+            ++gWordReads;
+            if (word != lastWord) {
+                IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: t=%llums slave-kernel=%#x ready=%u fatal=%u handover=%u stop_ack=%u\n",
+                      (unsigned long long)elapsedMs(began), word, unsigned(!!(word & QcomMssReady)),
+                      unsigned(!!(word & QcomMssFatal)), unsigned(!!(word & QcomMssHandover)), unsigned(!!(word & QcomMssStopAck)));
+                lastWord = word;
+            }
+            if (word & QcomMssFatal) { logCrash(smem); reason = "modem-fatal"; break; }
+        } else if (gWordSkipped++ < 8)
+            IOLog("THOR SERVE V237: modem entry sample skipped rc=%d t=%llums\n", remote,
+                  (unsigned long long)elapsedMs(began));
+        const uint64_t ms = elapsedMs(began);
+        if (!gDmsAsked && gHello && gIpcrtr && gIpcrtr->up && ms >= kQueryMs && (gDmsPeer || gUimPeer)) {
+            gDmsAsked = 1;
+            if (gDmsPeer) {
+                static const uint8_t opmode[7] = {0, 1, 0, 0x2d, 0, 0, 0};
+                (void)send(1, kModem, gDmsPeer, kDmsPort, opmode, sizeof opmode);
+            }
+            if (gUimPeer) {
+                static const uint8_t card[7] = {0, 2, 0, 0x2f, 0, 0, 0};
+                (void)send(1, kModem, gUimPeer, kUimPort, card, sizeof card);
+            }
+            IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: read-only queries sent dms=%u uim=%u\n", unsigned(!!gDmsPeer), unsigned(!!gUimPeer));
+        }
+        // Leave early once the four services that mark a finished init have been
+        // advertised and both read-only queries are answered.
+        if ((gServiceMask & wanted) == wanted && gDmsPeer && gUimPeer && gDmsAnswered && gUimAnswered) {
+            if (!settleAt) settleAt = unsigned(ms);
+            else if (ms - settleAt >= 3000) break;
+        }
+        if (ms >= kWatchMs) break;
+        if (ms >= nextReport) {
+            nextReport += 10000;
+            IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: t=%llums glink version=%u rx=%u tx=%u data=%u unknown_opens=%u '%s' ipcrtr_up=%u ctrl=%u servers=%#x "
+                  "pdm=%u rmtfs req=%u rd=%u/%llu wr=%u/%llu refused=%u pending=%u\n",
+                  (unsigned long long)ms, unsigned(gGlink.version_agreed), gGlink.rx_messages, gGlink.tx_messages,
+                  gGlink.rx_data, gGlink.unknown_opens, gGlink.unknown_names, gIpcrtr && gIpcrtr->up ? 1u : 0u, gCtlLogged,
+                  gServiceMask, gPdmRequests, gReqs, gReads, (unsigned long long)gReadBytes, gWrites,
+                  (unsigned long long)gWriteBytes, gRefused, pending());
+        }
+        IOSleep(ms < kEarlyMs ? 2 : 10);
+    }
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V237: modem entry samples read=%u skipped=%u\n", gWordReads, gWordSkipped);
+    IOLog("THOR SERVE V228: final=%s t=%llums hello=%u assigned=%u version=%u rx=%u tx=%u data=%u dropped=%u corrupt=%u unknown_opens=%u '%s' "
+          "servers=%u mask=%#x pdm=%u rmtfs req=%u rd=%u/%llu wr=%u/%llu refused=%u max_io=%llu dms=%u uim=%u\n",
+          reason, (unsigned long long)elapsedMs(began), unsigned(gHello), unsigned(gAssigned), unsigned(gGlink.version_agreed),
+          gGlink.rx_messages, gGlink.tx_messages, gGlink.rx_data, gGlink.dropped, gCorrupt, gGlink.unknown_opens, gGlink.unknown_names,
+          gServers, gServiceMask, gPdmRequests, gReqs, gReads, (unsigned long long)gReadBytes, gWrites,
+          (unsigned long long)gWriteBytes, gRefused, (unsigned long long)gMaxIoBytes, gDmsAnswered, gUimAnswered);
+    rfsTeardown();
+    return 0;
+}
+}  // namespace ThorServe
